WEBVTT

00:18.458 --> 00:21.040
Movie Screening Guidelines

00:21.041 --> 00:23.201
Movie Screening Guidelines
Don't raise the curtain yet!

00:24.666 --> 00:28.915
Welcome to this screening of theatrical
version of Movie: OVERLORD: The Sacred Kingdom.

00:29.916 --> 00:32.499
I extend my heartfelt
gratitude for your visit.

00:33.583 --> 00:34.457
Now, I must mention that this time,

00:34.458 --> 00:35.582
Now, l must mention that this time,

00:35.583 --> 00:41.124
OVERLORD: The Sacred Kingdom being
screened might be a bit intense for you.

00:42.041 --> 00:43.957
But don't worry.

00:44.625 --> 00:47.915
As I mentioned earlier, if you follow
the guidelines for the screening,

00:48.666 --> 00:50.582
your safety will be ensured,

00:52.791 --> 00:54.374
On the name of Ainz Ooal Gown...

00:54.500 --> 00:55.740
On the name of Ainz Ooal Gown..

00:55.958 --> 00:57.165
It's so cool, Ainz-sama!

00:57.250 --> 00:58.082
It's so cool, Ainz-sama!

00:58.250 --> 01:00.249
That was amazing, truly amazing Indeed!

01:01.625 --> 01:03.249
Is this the right vibe?

01:04.666 --> 01:07.790
Um, well then, let’s get started.

01:07.791 --> 01:08.791
Here we go.

01:10.750 --> 01:13.624
The use of mobile phones
during the screening is prohibited.

01:14.208 --> 01:16.374
Please turn them off or set them to silent.

01:16.625 --> 01:19.999
Failure to comply may result
in serious consequences.

01:21.375 --> 01:24.809
No loud noises or disturbances, especially
after death scenes, are strictly prohibited.

01:24.833 --> 01:28.165
Even if you see a shocking
scene, you mustn't scream or react.

01:28.500 --> 01:32.165
I can grant you eternal silence, you know.

01:32.875 --> 01:33.875
What!?

01:33.916 --> 01:38.207
Using flammable items in the theater and
bringing dangerous items are strictly forbidden.

01:38.333 --> 01:43.749
If you understand the difference in our power
levels, you wouldn't commit such foolish acts.

01:44.625 --> 01:49.540
Of course, it's obvious that you shouldn't kick the seat
in front of you or engage in any disruptive behavior.

01:50.416 --> 01:51.957
I might send you to the Hell.

01:52.458 --> 01:54.082
Wait, what does 'send to the hell' mean?

01:55.333 --> 01:57.915
Filming and recording during
the screening is prohibited.

01:59.916 --> 02:04.499
Movies are meant to be experienced
with your eyes, heart, and your whole body.

02:04.750 --> 02:09.499
With all your heart and
soul, feel the legend of Ainz.

02:10.458 --> 02:14.999
In the end, I hope
everyone enjoys this movie.

02:15.000 --> 02:16.374
That would be great.

02:25.500 --> 02:28.207
Animation

02:46.625 --> 02:48.017
In the year 2138 A.D, a once glorious DMMO-RPG
game Yggdrasil's service was about to end.

02:52.958 --> 02:53.374
One of the players, Satoru Suzuki, As the avatar "Momonga", quietly
awaited the end in the abandoned base, the Great Tomb of Nazarick.

02:53.375 --> 02:58.434
One of the players, Satoru Suzuki, As the avatar "Momonga", quietly
awaited the end in the abandoned base, the Great Tomb of Nazarick.

02:58.458 --> 03:03.778
However, for some reason, he did not log out even after the scheduled
time had passed and his skeleton avatar form remained the same.

03:05.958 --> 03:12.518
He might be alive somewhere, along with the NPCs who had now acquired a will of
their own. For the sake of his former companions, he called himself "Ainz Ooal Gown"

03:13.333 --> 03:14.040
- He founded a kingdom.

03:14.041 --> 03:18.374
The name of that kingdom is "The
Sorcerer Kingdom of Ainz Ooal Gown"...

03:21.708 --> 03:23.249
The Holy Kingdom of Roble.

03:24.083 --> 03:27.707
Its territory is divided into northern
and southern halves by a great gulf.

03:27.708 --> 03:30.749
With the Re-Estize Kingdom
located to the southwest,

03:30.750 --> 03:33.624
and to the east, it borders
the Slain Theocracy.

03:33.625 --> 03:37.249
The Abellion Hills spreading across the
border of empire are home to various species.

03:38.000 --> 03:45.374
To protect against invasions from diverse demihuman tribes,
they built a massive wall that runs across the peninsula.

03:47.166 --> 03:50.124
Frontline Central Base

04:04.875 --> 04:06.915
Orlando, it's time to change shifts.

04:08.083 --> 04:09.083
Where's your report?

04:10.416 --> 04:13.374
My apologies, Pabel Baraja.

04:13.916 --> 04:15.999
But there are no changes to report today.

04:16.625 --> 04:19.290
Wish I could see as clearly
in the dark as you can.

04:19.500 --> 04:21.999
I’d love to join you on the
Night watch someday, sir.

04:22.833 --> 04:25.207
My sharp eyesight was earned
through training, you know.

04:25.500 --> 04:27.915
You can achieve the same
thing if you work hard enough.

04:28.333 --> 04:31.332
I'd argue that it takes
talent to get results like that.

04:31.333 --> 04:33.707
A talent your daughter inherited, it seems.

04:34.500 --> 04:35.874
I'm so proud of her.

04:36.625 --> 04:38.540
She is gifted, if I do say so myself.

04:39.291 --> 04:42.499
Although it's unfortunate that she'
so dead set on becoming a paladin

04:43.000 --> 04:47.290
I'm sure that she simply wants to follow in her
mother's footsteps, which I can hardly object to.

04:47.875 --> 04:49.915
But she's no good when
it comes to swordplay.

04:50.375 --> 04:52.165
Her archery is excellent, however.

04:52.500 --> 04:55.415
So if she needs a career role
model, I sure wish she’d look to me.

04:55.750 --> 04:57.670
Did you know she's
still afraid of caterpillars?

04:57.708 --> 04:58.708
What a silly little girl.

05:05.541 --> 05:06.541
What is it?

05:08.166 --> 05:09.790
Demihumans, there's no doubt.

05:11.083 --> 05:12.083
Snakemen.

05:12.833 --> 05:14.040
How many, sir?

05:14.291 --> 05:15.665
It can't be a big deal.

05:16.416 --> 05:17.416
Right?

05:18.916 --> 05:20.540
They just keep piling up.

05:21.291 --> 05:22.957
And it's not just snakemen, either.

05:24.000 --> 05:25.207
This is bad news.

05:26.125 --> 05:27.125
There’s armats.

05:28.333 --> 05:29.333
And ogres.

05:30.375 --> 05:31.499
Are those caimans?

05:41.375 --> 05:42.375
An invasion?

05:43.041 --> 05:45.624
At this rate, we may need a
national mobilization order.

05:47.000 --> 05:49.749
I’ll take your word for
it, but I can’t see much.

05:50.208 --> 05:51.582
Have you spotted their leader yet?

05:52.166 --> 05:53.166
I don’t think so.

05:53.541 --> 05:55.999
Surely a commander of a
force that size would stick out.

05:56.000 --> 05:58.207
Take positions, men.

05:58.666 --> 06:00.040
And be prepared to fire.

06:02.041 --> 06:05.124
I think you should return to your
squad and wait for an update.

06:05.500 --> 06:06.124
Good idea.

06:06.291 --> 06:07.624
I’ll get on that right now.

06:08.041 --> 06:09.041
You be careful.

06:09.291 --> 06:11.832
Yes and you too.

06:17.458 --> 06:18.458
Neia.

06:28.750 --> 06:29.957
Should we shoot?

06:30.375 --> 06:34.582
They're still too far, but it won’t be
too long, so listen close for my order.

06:34.583 --> 06:37.124
I think I've spotted their leader.

06:42.916 --> 06:44.040
Stop right there!

06:44.875 --> 06:47.374
This is the territory of the
Roble Sacred Kingdom!

06:48.583 --> 06:50.790
Demi-humans like you
aren't allowed to set foot here!

06:50.791 --> 06:51.809
Demi-humans like you
aren’t allowed to set foot here!

06:51.833 --> 06:53.207
Disperse immediately!

06:56.416 --> 06:58.999
Greetings, citizens of the Sacred Kingdom.

06:59.708 --> 07:01.374
Allow me to introduce myself.

07:02.041 --> 07:04.165
My name is Jaldabaoth.

07:04.291 --> 07:07.124
You mean the Great Demon Jaldabaoth?

07:08.291 --> 07:10.290
You know of me. How flattening.

07:11.625 --> 07:17.499
I am indeed the one who orc-hestrated the grand feast in
Re-Estize’s kingdom that was met with such rapturous applause.

07:18.375 --> 07:26.375
However, if I must be given such a grandiose title,
I would prefer to be called Demon King Jaldabaoth.

07:28.083 --> 07:30.374
Demon King Jaldabaoth...

07:31.666 --> 07:35.249
I’ve come here to make
your kingdom a living hell.

07:36.250 --> 07:40.874
Wails, maledictions, and cries
of pain will echo without end.

07:41.625 --> 07:43.665
It will become a carnival of suffering.

07:45.333 --> 07:47.749
You think we would ever allow such a thing?

07:48.791 --> 07:51.957
This is not simply the Sacred
Kingdom'firstline of defense.

07:52.166 --> 07:53.874
It is the only one that is required!

07:53.875 --> 07:58.332
This wall guarantees the peace of
every last person who dwells behind it!

07:58.666 --> 08:01.124
It shall not be shaken, even before you!

08:05.041 --> 08:06.874
Let's find out, shall we?

08:19.375 --> 08:22.624
Now, allow me to
offer you a gift in return.

08:23.166 --> 08:26.832
Tenth-tier magic, Meteor Fall

08:53.708 --> 08:56.332
Take your sword and
drive it through your throat!

09:11.000 --> 09:13.624
Get here a bit faster next time.

09:17.250 --> 09:20.874
I have no further critiques,
so please begin the attack.

09:34.875 --> 09:35.875
Come, demons.

09:38.833 --> 09:40.832
Your job is to support t^he demihumans.

09:41.833 --> 09:45.540
Also, find an appropriate way to
drive the humans from the stronghold.

09:45.541 --> 09:45.874
You may kill some of them,
but don't get c-arried away.

09:46.000 --> 09:48.415
You may kill some of them,
but don't get carried away.

09:49.000 --> 09:50.374
We need a few to escape.

09:56.333 --> 09:56.874
Good.

09:57.291 --> 09:59.499
Everything is proceeding according to plan.

10:00.208 --> 10:05.415
<i>That said, I'm sure the outcome my lord orchestrates
will be far beyond even my wildest conjectures.</i>

10:05.916 --> 10:11.582
There is no greater joy than observing his genius in
action, and no greater lesson in how better to serve him.

10:13.166 --> 10:15.707
What more could I ask for in this world?

10:22.083 --> 10:28.999
OVERLORD: The Sacred Kingdom

10:34.000 --> 10:37.665
Kalinsha

10:51.166 --> 10:52.582
The Grandmaster Remedios!

10:52.958 --> 10:57.165
If you turn right once more from this street, you
will reach the square where Jaldabaoth is waiting!

10:57.166 --> 10:58.166
I see.

10:58.250 --> 11:01.957
In that case, begin casting any
long-lasting defense spells immediately.

11:02.333 --> 11:03.333
Yes, ma'am

11:04.208 --> 11:05.290
Follow me!

11:17.375 --> 11:19.624
Prepare yourselves, Jaldabaoth!

11:25.416 --> 11:26.416
Take cover!

11:26.916 --> 11:27.832
You’d better leave him to me!

11:27.833 --> 11:28.953
You'd better leave him to me

11:30.208 --> 11:32.707
Are you a paladin or a raging bull?

11:33.250 --> 11:34.999
Perhaps my red tie provoked you.

11:41.208 --> 11:43.874
Are you the one who calls
himself the Demon King?

11:44.416 --> 11:45.416
Indeed.

11:45.791 --> 11:48.124
And are you the princess
who became Holy Queen?

11:48.833 --> 11:50.374
Yes, I am indeed'

11:50.375 --> 11:53.999
Please, Princess Calca, there's no
need to offer your name to this monster.

11:54.500 --> 11:56.832
We’ve confirmed his identity
and that’s more than enough.

11:57.125 --> 11:58.624
All that's left is to kill him.

11:58.625 --> 12:00.225
Remedios, please, just give me a moment.

12:00.250 --> 12:02.290
Sister, come on, show some patience.

12:02.500 --> 12:04.499
Princess Galea's trying
to gather information.

12:06.041 --> 12:08.915
Tell me, what is your purpose
appearing before us alone?

12:09.125 --> 12:12.832
If you want to conquer this country, why
did you leave your army behind this time?

12:13.875 --> 12:18.999
I assume that you've heard of the
Adamantite-class adventurer, Momon of Darkness?

12:19.000 --> 12:25.082
My plans for the Re-Estize's kingdom failed due
to the efforts of that powerful warrior alone.

12:26.333 --> 12:32.749
If there is anyone in this kingdom with strength on his level, then
it's reasonable to assume that they would be guarding the holy queen.

12:33.416 --> 12:35.457
Although it seems my
concerns were without merit.

12:35.458 --> 12:36.517
Although it seems my
concerns were without merit.

12:36.541 --> 12:37.541
I had to check.

12:38.208 --> 12:38.832
Are those maids...

12:38.833 --> 12:42.153
So this is the strongest paladin in the
history of the Sacred Order, a Grandmaster?

12:42.208 --> 12:43.208
How disappointing.

12:43.791 --> 12:44.832
How dare you!

12:45.208 --> 12:47.540
Try saying that again
after I take off your head!

12:47.541 --> 12:48.541
Control yourself!

12:48.666 --> 12:50.106
You’re just letting him provoke you!

12:50.291 --> 12:53.624
Well, Holy princess, is there
anything else you wanted to ask?

12:55.125 --> 12:56.125
No, that is all.

12:57.041 --> 12:58.041
The time’s come.

12:58.541 --> 12:59.832
Remember this, Remedios.

13:00.208 --> 13:02.374
You are the sword that protects this land!

13:02.833 --> 13:05.290
You are the justice that empowers the weak!

13:06.625 --> 13:10.374
No matter what, we cannot allow
further harm to come to our people!

13:11.208 --> 13:12.540
Angel unit, forward!

13:25.166 --> 13:27.332
Flow Acceleration!

13:29.500 --> 13:31.040
Holy Strike!

13:33.333 --> 13:34.915
I see.

13:37.416 --> 13:38.040
Casting Penetrate Magic, Holy Ray!

13:38.041 --> 13:40.332
Casting Penetrate Magic, Holy Ray!

13:41.625 --> 13:45.249
Casting Twin Penetrate Magic, Holy Ray!

13:48.375 --> 13:50.499
The angels need to
coordinate their attacks!

13:50.625 --> 13:51.625
Stay focused!

13:51.666 --> 13:52.915
That's good advice.

13:53.291 --> 13:56.040
Even insects can be
aggravating in a proper swarm.

14:10.458 --> 14:11.540
Not enough!

14:11.666 --> 14:12.290
You did it!

14:12.541 --> 14:13.165
Not yet!

14:13.541 --> 14:15.249
Destroy the building, but stay away!

14:16.958 --> 14:17.958
Fireball!

14:26.250 --> 14:28.124
You've proven yourself a nuisance.

14:31.958 --> 14:34.749
It seems I'll have to put
some effort into this battle.

14:35.250 --> 14:37.457
Assuming you don't die from shock, that is.

14:48.833 --> 14:49.957
Ready your angels!

14:50.166 --> 14:51.540
All priests, attack at once!

15:04.333 --> 15:05.540
Princess Calca!

15:06.250 --> 15:07.499
Maintain a safe distance!'

15:15.500 --> 15:17.540
You have to run away

15:17.958 --> 15:19.124
We can't defeat them

15:19.333 --> 15:20.499
At least not like this!

15:23.000 --> 15:24.999
If they live, the kingdom lives.

15:25.291 --> 15:26.291
That’s enough.

15:28.916 --> 15:29.916
Greater Teleportation!

15:36.666 --> 15:39.415
Get away from her.

15:42.250 --> 15:46.624
Princess Calca!

16:01.333 --> 16:03.957
I don't sense the presence of any monsters.

16:04.875 --> 16:08.082
Still, it may be safer to stay here
a moment until the fog c-clears.

16:08.875 --> 16:09.875
Would Dad wait?

16:11.791 --> 16:12.791
Neia Ba raja!

16:13.291 --> 16:14.291
Uh, yes?

16:23.500 --> 16:25.499
What in the world is happening here?

16:25.875 --> 16:27.332
Can you explain this fog?

16:27.333 --> 16:29.249
I'm afraid I can't, ma'am.

16:29.708 --> 16:30.915
It defies all reason.

16:31.666 --> 16:36.332
To start, there are no bodies of water nearby,
so there shouldn't be such thick fog around here.

16:36.833 --> 16:39.749
Since we don’t know the cause,
we should watch and wait...

16:39.750 --> 16:40.750
for now.

16:41.000 --> 16:42.249
You’re utterly useless.

16:42.458 --> 16:43.618
Don’t blame her, Grandmaster.

16:43.791 --> 16:45.874
Squire Baraja has been a tremendous help.

16:46.166 --> 16:50.707
We were able to avoid the demi-humans who have
overrun our kingdom thanks to her and her sharp eyes.

16:50.875 --> 16:52.665
We owe our safe travels here to her.

16:52.666 --> 16:54.207
That's not the point!

16:54.666 --> 16:56.707
We can’t afford to waste time, Gustav!

16:56.916 --> 17:00.749
Every moment that we stall is another moment
that our people are being oppressed and killed!

17:09.250 --> 17:10.332
What is that?

17:13.791 --> 17:14.332
But..

17:14.333 --> 17:15.499
We’re on land.

17:16.958 --> 17:18.249
It can't be!

17:19.666 --> 17:22.165
Is this some sort of illusion, or what?

17:45.041 --> 17:46.041
Oh...

17:59.791 --> 18:00.791
Amazing.

18:06.583 --> 18:10.999
No mistaking it, this is the
sorcerer kingdom of Ainz Ooal Gown.

18:11.333 --> 18:15.249
What a repulsive statue, to
think that monster is their king.

18:16.125 --> 18:20.165
Your feelings aside, please remember that
we're asking this kingdom for their help.

18:20.500 --> 18:23.374
Momon of Darkness is the only
one who can best Jaldabaoth.

18:23.708 --> 18:25.957
If they won’t lend his
service to us, there’s no hope.

18:26.125 --> 18:27.790
We are at this undead's mercy.

18:27.791 --> 18:30.415
I'm well aware of our situation, Gustav.

18:30.666 --> 18:32.415
No humiliation is worse than failure.

18:32.833 --> 18:34.499
I would do anything to save our home.

18:34.833 --> 18:37.874
That includes bowing to a
filthy undead so don’t you worry.

18:38.416 --> 18:40.832
We are the paladin order,
serving the sacred princess!

18:41.250 --> 18:42.665
Chin up, and back straight!

18:42.958 --> 18:43.958
Raise up our flag!

18:58.750 --> 19:02.332
Welcome to the sorcerer
kingdom of Ainz Ooal Gown.

19:02.333 --> 19:05.999
My name is Riraba Yusvenya Ain Darun.

19:06.208 --> 19:07.208
I'm a naga.

19:07.500 --> 19:12.332
Our king is aware of your desperrate situation and
is willing to grant you an audience right away.

19:13.083 --> 19:17.874
However, there are some important details about
this city that you must be made aware of beforehand.

19:20.333 --> 19:21.333
A dragon?

19:21.708 --> 19:22.708
There's no panic.

19:22.875 --> 19:25.832
You mean to tell me dragons
are treated like citizens here too?

19:26.000 --> 19:27.000
Indeed they, are!

19:27.125 --> 19:28.832
But that's nothing special in the least.

19:28.958 --> 19:31.874
You'll find any number of races
walking this kingdom's streets.

19:32.750 --> 19:34.374
Including the undead.

19:45.000 --> 19:46.790
Everything seems rather peaceful.

20:20.000 --> 20:23.165
Representatives from the sacred
kingdom, we welcome you all.

20:23.625 --> 20:26.040
To begin, please allow
me to introduce myself.

20:26.208 --> 20:27.208
I’m the prime minister.

20:27.708 --> 20:31.332
In other words. I'm overseer of the
floor and territorial guardians here.

20:31.375 --> 20:33.249
My name is Albedo.

20:33.958 --> 20:36.749
Ah, I thank you for giving
us such a cordial greeting.

20:37.416 --> 20:40.332
From the sacred kingdom,
my name is Remedios Custodio.

20:40.625 --> 20:42.499
I'm the leader of the sacred paladin order.

20:43.291 --> 20:46.249
We're truly honored your king has
granted us an audience so quickly.

20:46.750 --> 20:48.082
You have my deepest gratitude.

20:48.458 --> 20:50.165
No need for thanks, I assure you.

20:50.875 --> 20:52.790
His majesty has been terribly concerned.

20:53.125 --> 20:55.624
The state of the sacred
kingdom is quite troubling indeed.

20:55.625 --> 20:57.749
I spoke to him about it personally.

20:58.625 --> 21:03.499
Given the urgency of your kingdom's situation,
it’s only natural that he would make time for you.

21:03.916 --> 21:04.665
Yes, that's very charitable of him.

21:04.666 --> 21:06.582
Yes, that's very charitable of him.

21:09.333 --> 21:10.582
His majesty will now enter.

21:12.375 --> 21:13.790
Everyone, bow your heads.

21:16.833 --> 21:20.290
I present to you the great
sorcerer king, Ainz Ooal Gown.

21:32.583 --> 21:34.415
You may now raise your heads.

21:44.041 --> 21:45.332
I'm honored.

21:48.041 --> 21:52.499
It must have been quite the journey for
you, coming from the far-off sacred kingdom.

21:52.500 --> 21:54.309
It must have been quite the journey for
you, coming from the far-off sacred kingdom.

21:54.333 --> 21:56.374
And for your paladins as well.

21:58.000 --> 22:02.707
So he's undead king, Ains Ooal Gown.

22:06.125 --> 22:07.125
Squire Baraja!

22:07.500 --> 22:10.082
What were you thinking,
speaking to the king like that?!

22:10.083 --> 22:11.915
Grandmaster, please let her go!

22:11.916 --> 22:15.540
I understand that Squire Baraja
spoke without permission back there.

22:15.708 --> 22:20.082
But think, she convinced the king to send Momon
to our country in two years instead of three.

22:20.625 --> 22:22.749
So shouldn't you be praising her instead?

22:22.750 --> 22:24.165
Do you know what you’re saying?!

22:24.166 --> 22:26.374
The entire negotiation
could have fallen apart!

22:27.291 --> 22:31.124
Listen, regardless of the result, we can't
praise someone for acting out like that!

22:31.250 --> 22:32.707
I'm very sorry, Grandmaster.

22:33.500 --> 22:36.040
And what exactly do you
think that apology is worth?

22:36.500 --> 22:38.290
What if they were
offended and sent us away?

22:38.541 --> 22:40.457
How would you take responsibility for that?

22:40.458 --> 22:42.332
I’d pay with my life.

22:42.750 --> 22:44.499
If this failed, we'd all be dead anyway.

22:44.708 --> 22:48.457
So if the Sorcerer King didn't agree, you
might as well offer my head to apologize.

22:50.375 --> 22:52.874
You think your measly
life is worth that much?!

22:52.875 --> 22:54.624
And you think I'd just agree to kill you?!

22:55.166 --> 22:56.832
No, you are tempting me.

22:57.333 --> 22:59.415
Grandmaster, I believe
you've made your point.

22:59.708 --> 23:02.207
We couldn’t have held out
three whole years for Momon.

23:10.833 --> 23:11.957
Neia Baraja.

23:12.458 --> 23:14.957
You showed incredible resolve back there.

23:15.500 --> 23:19.582
The Grandmaster may be harsh with you, but
she does recognize what you accomplished.

23:20.333 --> 23:24.415
As for what’s next, well try to
renegotiate with the Sorcerer King soon.

23:25.250 --> 23:31.624
The Grandmaster is anxious, but this kind of negotiation often
requires several meetings to find a good outcome for both sides.

23:32.250 --> 23:33.665
I understand your impatience.

23:33.916 --> 23:36.707
It felt like our only hope was
crumbling right before our eyes.

23:36.708 --> 23:41.790
Still, the Grandmaster knows you only spoke
up out of concern for the Sacred Kingdom.

23:42.375 --> 23:47.082
The thing is, she's carrying the entire weight
of our nation's future on her back right now.

23:47.791 --> 23:48.999
You should be told the truth.

23:49.583 --> 23:52.582
You don't know what happened when
the Sacred Princess faced Jaldabaoth.

23:52.958 --> 23:56.878
I assume you’ve only heard what was reported since
you weren't at the battle in Kalinsha, correct?

23:57.291 --> 23:58.291
Correct.

23:58.583 --> 24:00.874
We were very particular
about what was said.

24:01.500 --> 24:06.332
As far as other countries know, the North was taken
by the Demi-Human Alliance, but the South is safe.

24:06.333 --> 24:10.540
The Princess and her forces maintain high
morale despite their loss, and that's it.

24:11.583 --> 24:12.583
Is that not true?

24:16.500 --> 24:18.374
We must get Momon's help.

24:19.166 --> 24:20.999
We can't leave here empty-handed.

24:24.000 --> 24:25.124
Greater teleportation.

24:31.916 --> 24:33.582
Get away from her!

24:40.833 --> 24:42.874
You’ll make a fine weapon.

24:51.666 --> 24:52.666
No!

24:57.250 --> 24:58.874
Let her go.

25:00.250 --> 25:01.665
Stop it!

25:03.000 --> 25:04.999
Let her go!

25:08.916 --> 25:09.916
Enough!

25:22.458 --> 25:23.957
What do I do now?

25:26.583 --> 25:28.332
That’s quite the heavy burden.

25:29.958 --> 25:30.958
Huh?

25:34.916 --> 25:37.624
This is Squire Neia Baraja,
please open the door.

25:38.875 --> 25:40.540
Excuse me ma'am, the
Sorcerer King is here to see you.

25:42.750 --> 25:44.290
He wishes to speak in secrecy.

25:47.541 --> 25:47.999
What

25:48.166 --> 25:49.166
Have you gone insane?

25:49.500 --> 25:51.249
No need for any of that.

25:52.833 --> 25:54.499
It’s not the girl’s fault.

25:54.833 --> 25:57.749
If you have an issue, take it up with me.

26:01.541 --> 26:03.332
Do pardon the sudden visit.

26:03.958 --> 26:06.207
There are certain things I
cannot speak of in public.

26:07.083 --> 26:08.457
This requires a bit of discretion.

26:09.291 --> 26:13.499
For example, there is a reason why I
cannot send Momon to help you right now.

26:14.166 --> 26:16.665
It has not been long since
the founding of my kingdom.

26:17.291 --> 26:19.124
I am hardly a typical ruler, as
non-dead humans tend to fear me.

26:22.583 --> 26:26.624
However, the presence of a reliable
hero like Momon puts their hearts at ease.

26:27.166 --> 26:29.832
If he were to leave, I fear
that my people might suffer.

26:31.208 --> 26:32.707
That said, there may be a solution.

26:33.291 --> 26:34.415
I have one demand.

26:34.833 --> 26:39.749
If you can fulfill it, I would be willing to grant you
the services of someone equal in strength to Momon.

26:40.083 --> 26:41.083
Do you mean that?

26:41.208 --> 26:42.665
What is your demand, your majesty?

26:42.833 --> 26:44.832
I fear we have little to offer right now.

26:45.250 --> 26:46.457
I want maids.

26:48.875 --> 26:50.749
Specific ones, that is.

26:50.958 --> 26:52.999
I’m afraid you've lost me.

26:53.041 --> 26:55.915
I recall seeing demon maids
accompanying Jaldabaoth.

26:56.166 --> 26:57.446
Is that who you’re referring to?

26:57.583 --> 26:57.999
Yes.

26:58.541 --> 27:00.499
Before I continue, let me ask.

27:00.750 --> 27:02.207
How much do you know about magic?

27:02.708 --> 27:03.999
Next to nothing, I'd say.

27:04.700 --> 27:05.700
I see.

27:06.000 --> 27:12.624
Well, in simple terms, I suspect that Jaldabaoth is
controlling those maids with some sort of magical contract.

27:13.291 --> 27:17.457
If he is defeated and the contract
taken, I can command the maids.

27:17.791 --> 27:19.332
They are known to be powerful servants.

27:19.333 --> 27:22.290
I believe they would be a great
boon to the Sorcerer Kingdom.

27:23.000 --> 27:24.000
I understand.

27:24.250 --> 27:25.730
Then well hand the maids over to you.

27:26.583 --> 27:30.040
That said, I'm surprised there's someone
who compares to Momon in strength.

27:30.250 --> 27:31.330
Can you tell me a bit more?

27:31.541 --> 27:32.541
It's me.

27:34.291 --> 27:38.374
Considering the nature of my request, I don't
think this should come as such a surprise.

27:39.041 --> 27:42.540
And in case you have any concern,
I am even stronger than Momon.

27:43.041 --> 27:44.832
Then I have no objections at all.

27:45.000 --> 27:46.000
You sure?

27:46.541 --> 27:48.040
I won't be bringing any help.

27:48.041 --> 27:53.707
Also, I can teleport to any place that I've
been before, so I will come and go as I please.

27:54.291 --> 27:55.291
I see.

27:55.625 --> 27:56.999
Do you want an army as well?

27:57.541 --> 27:59.957
Though I warn you, they will be undead.

28:00.375 --> 28:01.375
There’s no need.

28:01.791 --> 28:05.874
As long as you truly possess enough power to
defeat Jaldabaoth, then I’ll be satisfied.

28:06.625 --> 28:08.374
Well handle his forces ourselves.

28:09.125 --> 28:10.332
When can you depart?

28:10.500 --> 28:11.500
Tomorrow morning.

28:12.139 --> 28:12.417
Excellent.

28:12.441 --> 28:13.441
Wait, no?

28:14.375 --> 28:15.375
Let’s discuss this!

28:18.333 --> 28:19.874
What in the world are you thinking?

28:19.875 --> 28:22.874
The fact that he's
undead aside, he's a king!

28:23.208 --> 28:25.374
You'd have him fight
Jaldabaoth to the death?

28:25.708 --> 28:26.708
What do you suggest?

28:26.750 --> 28:28.415
Accepting his undead army instead

28:28.750 --> 28:30.999
Our people would be,
terrified and our land tainted.

28:31.291 --> 28:32.874
He's not just a sorcerer.

28:32.958 --> 28:34.358
He's the ruler of a foreign nation.

28:34.708 --> 28:36.665
What if he gets injured
or even worse, killed?

28:37.708 --> 28:39.499
King or not, he's a monster, right?

28:40.208 --> 28:43.624
Whether he dies or the demon
dies, it's hardly any concern to us.

28:44.166 --> 28:45.166
Wouldn't you say?

28:47.875 --> 28:50.249
My point is, they’re
both enemies of mankind.

28:50.250 --> 28:54.707
To be frank, if they wipe each other
out, that would be the best case scenario.

28:57.000 --> 28:58.124
You mean that?

28:58.625 --> 29:00.624
Does that embody the spirit of justice?

29:01.375 --> 29:01.832
Of course

29:02.083 --> 29:04.003
Because it would save
the lives of the innocent!

29:05.583 --> 29:06.957
Squire Neia Baraja

29:07.500 --> 29:08.500
Yes, ma’am

29:08.541 --> 29:10.957
You will accompany the Sorcerer King.

29:11.958 --> 29:16.332
Stay by his side at all times and convince
him to be useful to us any way you can.

29:16.541 --> 29:19.124
But don’t provide too
much intel about our home.

29:19.875 --> 29:21.832
Sweet-talk him and
make sure he stays happy.

29:22.166 --> 29:23.749
Then well milk him for all he’s worth.

29:43.416 --> 29:44.790
What should I do?

29:45.083 --> 29:48.374
I've never been the attendant of
a king, let alone an undead one.

29:49.541 --> 29:51.332
Perhaps I should start up a conversation?

29:52.250 --> 29:54.832
But if I displease him,
I'm afraid he might kill me.

29:58.541 --> 30:00.040
There's something on my face.

30:00.291 --> 30:01.790
You seem to be glaring at it.

30:02.166 --> 30:04.540
No, please excuse my
rudeness, your majesty!

30:05.416 --> 30:06.416
No offense taken.

30:06.750 --> 30:08.874
But are you uncomfortable
riding with an undead?

30:09.458 --> 30:10.624
Not at all, your majesty!

30:11.000 --> 30:12.957
By the way, I wasn't glaring.

30:13.083 --> 30:14.999
I inherited these fierce
eyes from my father.

30:15.875 --> 30:16.875
Is that so.

30:18.833 --> 30:21.749
I do wish there was
something we could talk about.

30:22.833 --> 30:25.082
Ah, I know your visit was short.

30:25.541 --> 30:26.981
But what did you think of my country

30:27.625 --> 30:30.665
It may have felt small in the eyes of
someone from the Sacred Kingdom.

30:31.333 --> 30:34.124
It seemed like a wonderful
place; peaceful and happy.

30:34.625 --> 30:38.207
And it was the first time I’ve ever seen
so many different races living together.

30:38.416 --> 30:39.874
Good, that's good.

30:40.083 --> 30:42.540
Also, the statues of you
were very impressive.

30:42.916 --> 30:44.582
They certainly are big.

30:45.375 --> 30:46.874
Ah, yes, that they are.

30:47.458 --> 30:49.582
My subordinates insisted upon making them.

30:50.125 --> 30:53.124
On top of that, we're planning
to build more of them elsewhere.

30:54.458 --> 30:55.749
That's so nice

30:56.083 --> 30:59.374
Then people outside of the capital
can witness your greatness too, right?

31:00.083 --> 31:01.332
Ah, I see.

31:02.083 --> 31:03.832
That’s what my subordinates think too.

31:04.833 --> 31:06.290
But I'm not certain that I agree.

31:07.000 --> 31:08.874
I think it might be a bit short-sighted.

31:09.250 --> 31:10.540
What do you mean by that?

31:12.916 --> 31:16.040
The true greatness of a king
cannot be shown in monuments.

31:16.583 --> 31:18.249
It must be shown through his actions.

31:20.958 --> 31:24.665
I want to be known for the peace
and prosperity created under my rule.

31:25.458 --> 31:27.332
That is what I want people to see.

31:27.500 --> 31:28.500
How wise.

31:28.625 --> 31:30.374
You truly are a fine king.

31:31.500 --> 31:36.082
By the way, how long will it take for us
to reach the Sacred Kingdom by carriage?

31:36.291 --> 31:37.832
About ten days, I think.

31:38.875 --> 31:39.875
A while, then.

31:40.250 --> 31:43.499
In that case, I would like to
learn more about you, Miss Baraja.

31:44.208 --> 31:47.749
Perhaps you could begin by telling me
why you decided to become a paladin.

31:47.750 --> 31:51.999
I would be honored to tell you,
though you may find it boring.

32:01.541 --> 32:04.582
Do accept my most humble
apologies, Your Majesty.

32:05.166 --> 32:12.165
I know this is hardly a proper place to welcome someone such as you,
but please join us in the meeting room so that we may discuss our plans.

32:12.875 --> 32:13.875
Of course.

32:18.375 --> 32:22.374
Since our situation has changed, let's determine
what our new course of action should be.

32:22.375 --> 32:28.290
Before that, since I've agreed to help you, I think I should
know the full details of what's happening in your kingdom.

32:32.000 --> 32:36.332
Seeing as we're meeting in a cave,
things must be quite dire for your army.

32:37.666 --> 32:43.749
It's clear that your north and south are separated geographically,
but I'm aware that a political'divide exists as well.

32:44.416 --> 32:48.165
Am I correct to assume that you will
receive no aid from the Southern Territory?

32:48.166 --> 32:52.832
Also, Princess Calca's absence
today can only mean one thing, I fear.

32:54.291 --> 32:57.124
I can't believe you’d know
so much at mere glance.

32:58.041 --> 32:59.041
Well then..

33:00.958 --> 33:03.374
Sacred Princess Calca
is missing, it's true.

33:03.916 --> 33:05.582
Our High Priestess Kelart as well.

33:05.916 --> 33:09.832
They faced Jaldabaoth, but we separated
when the battle took a turn for the worse.

33:11.458 --> 33:15.874
However, they use high-tier priestly
magic, so those two are far from helpless.

33:15.875 --> 33:20.332
Although there's a good chance they’ve been
captured, I have faith that they’re still alive.

33:21.541 --> 33:25.749
Searching for them is a major priority,
as is the liberation of our cities.

33:26.125 --> 33:29.665
Our hope is to free our captured citizens
and bolster our dwindling supplies.

33:30.458 --> 33:33.332
Not far from here, there is
a small city named Loyts.

33:33.875 --> 33:37.749
We’ve obtained information the people of
the royal family, may be imprisoned there.

33:38.666 --> 33:42.290
If that news is true, we need
to rescue them right away.

33:42.291 --> 33:42.790
This should-be a simple
task with a powerful

33:42.791 --> 33:47.082
This should be a simple task with a powerful
magic caster like Your Majesty on our side.

33:47.500 --> 33:51.749
If you, or we, attack now, we'll
make short order of the enemy.

33:52.125 --> 33:54.332
You're worth ten thousand
troops on your own.

33:54.875 --> 33:56.499
I cannot meet your expectations.

33:57.708 --> 33:59.040
You mean you won't fight?

33:59.708 --> 34:00.249
Correct.

34:00.458 --> 34:02.749
Or that is to say, I will
only fight Jaldabaoth.

34:03.416 --> 34:05.457
That is the only reason
I have come after all.

34:06.208 --> 34:10.165
He will be a formidable foe, so I must
conserve my magic if I hope to defeat him.

34:10.958 --> 34:11.958
Oh, I see.

34:12.791 --> 34:14.624
This is the Sacred Kingdom’s war to wage.

34:14.833 --> 34:18.540
I won't interfere with your affairs,
but I won't follow your orders either.

34:19.958 --> 34:24.249
If you want me to stand at the forefront
of this operation, then I must lead.

34:24.666 --> 34:28.040
In which case, you and your forces
would be placed under my command.

34:29.125 --> 34:35.665
Once that happened, I could negotiate with the nobles of the Southern
Territory and use the best possible means to save this kingdom.

34:36.333 --> 34:39.040
As far as we know, the
sacred Princess is still our ruler.

34:39.041 --> 34:43.624
Regardless of the situation, we cannot
fall under the command of another kingdom.

34:59.291 --> 35:02.290
Miss Baraja, your steps
were unusually quiet.

35:02.708 --> 35:04.832
Especially for someone
trained to be a paladin.

35:05.791 --> 35:06.791
My apologies.

35:07.333 --> 35:11.582
My father was a ranger, so he taught me how to
use silent footwork when I was just a child.

35:12.083 --> 35:15.415
If I recall correctly, you did mention
that he was skilled with a bow.

35:15.875 --> 35:17.874
Did he impart that
knowledge to you as well?

35:17.875 --> 35:24.040
I do have a bit of experience, but that doesn't
serve me since paladins only fight with swords.

35:24.208 --> 35:25.249
Those are the rules.

35:26.041 --> 35:27.041
What a waste.

35:28.083 --> 35:29.749
A paladin with a bow.

35:30.208 --> 35:33.290
Interesting combinations open
the path to rare job classes.

35:33.750 --> 35:35.457
Yes, I like it.

35:35.750 --> 35:38.457
Oh, um, thank you, your majesty.

35:39.166 --> 35:40.166
Let me see.

35:44.416 --> 35:46.582
How about I lend you this?

35:46.583 --> 35:51.707
As I’m likely to cause you trouble during this
endeavor, you may consider it a token of my gratitude.

35:52.625 --> 35:54.999
I can't accept such a fine gift from you!

35:55.166 --> 35:57.540
And you don't owe a thing
to a commoner like me!

35:57.916 --> 36:01.124
Whether it was an order or
not, you're taking care of me.

36:01.750 --> 36:05.124
What station you have in life does
not affect my appreciation of that.

36:06.125 --> 36:07.125
Your majesty.

36:08.458 --> 36:10.749
This is Ultimate Shooting Star Super.

36:12.333 --> 36:15.499
I can't say I've ever seen a
bow with such an elaborate name.

36:16.333 --> 36:18.749
Sounds like a weapon that
would appear in ancient myths.

36:19.250 --> 36:20.999
Actually, you’re not far off the mark.

36:21.375 --> 36:25.207
This bow was made with rune
technology, an ancient and powerful art.

36:25.666 --> 36:28.832
I want you to use it to protect
me should the need arise.

36:34.333 --> 36:35.790
I accept your gift.

36:36.291 --> 36:41.582
And though I may be of humble skill, I swear to
protect you to the best of my ability, with loyalty.

36:42.208 --> 36:44.624
Until you see this great
endeavor to its end.

36:52.041 --> 36:53.041
Onward

36:53.166 --> 36:54.415
Yes.

36:58.708 --> 37:01.374
Small City: Lyots

37:02.916 --> 37:04.165
How valiant.

37:04.875 --> 37:05.875
Indeed.

37:06.000 --> 37:09.124
Our paladins charge fearlessly
into battle to protect the innocent.

37:10.041 --> 37:11.832
And yet...

37:19.666 --> 37:20.457
This is the end.

37:20.458 --> 37:23.832
Thus begins our battle, to free this
kingdom from Jaldabaoth's clutches!

37:24.375 --> 37:25.375
For justice!

37:25.708 --> 37:26.708
For justice!

37:46.708 --> 37:49.957
Uh, by the way.

37:50.625 --> 37:52.415
Are you not joining
the battle, Miss Baraja?

37:53.166 --> 37:55.374
The runes on that bow
imbue it with great power.

37:55.750 --> 37:57.749
I’m sure you would see outstanding results.

37:57.916 --> 37:58.582
I couldn’t.

37:58.833 --> 38:00.540
I’m your majesty's attendant, right?

38:01.083 --> 38:02.083
Y-Yes.

38:02.666 --> 38:06.249
Speaking of the bow, did any of the
paladins happen to take notice of it?

38:06.750 --> 38:08.332
Perhaps they asked to borrow it.

38:08.833 --> 38:11.499
Always they had swords engraved with runes.

38:11.833 --> 38:12.999
No, nothing of the sort.

38:13.416 --> 38:15.582
That is to say, they took
interest in it, of course.

38:15.791 --> 38:18.991
But I assured them it wasn't something
they could ever hope to receive from you.

38:20.750 --> 38:22.624
Yes, very well then.

38:22.708 --> 38:23.708
Stand back.

38:24.166 --> 38:26.290
Move away from the wall, humans.

38:27.708 --> 38:28.790
This is bad.

38:30.250 --> 38:32.874
I'll kill this child if
you take another step

38:33.000 --> 38:34.957
And there's more where he came from, too!

38:36.958 --> 38:38.374
That filthy coward.

38:38.625 --> 38:39.374
Move back!

38:39.500 --> 38:40.582
Do as he says

38:42.750 --> 38:45.290
And put down those
weapons while you're at it!

38:45.750 --> 38:48.665
Surrender without trouble
and we will spare your lives!

38:51.791 --> 38:52.915
Grandmaster Custodio.

38:54.041 --> 38:55.124
This won't do.

38:55.625 --> 38:59.665
If you teach the enemy that hostages are
effective, they will continue using them.

38:59.791 --> 39:01.790
Do you think I haven't realized that?

39:01.916 --> 39:02.916
Please calm down.

39:02.958 --> 39:04.124
We cannot lose focus

39:04.125 --> 39:05.249
Our goal is right there!

39:05.583 --> 39:06.082
Shame on you!

39:06.375 --> 39:08.249
You’ve lost your sense
of justice so quickly!

39:09.000 --> 39:11.624
I ask you, who did you
pledge your sword to?

39:12.875 --> 39:14.999
What would Princess Calca do right now?

39:15.500 --> 39:16.832
She cares for all of her people.

39:17.166 --> 39:19.290
She would never
sacrifice the life of a child.

39:19.541 --> 39:20.832
She'd find a better way!

39:21.416 --> 39:22.416
Her justice!

39:22.916 --> 39:23.916
Her wish!

39:24.666 --> 39:26.207
Are you telling me that it's wrong?

39:29.000 --> 39:32.290
If you're radiant in failure,
all of this is meaningless.

39:32.291 --> 39:36.040
We won't fail, and we won't bring
dishonor to Princess Calca either!

39:36.500 --> 39:38.457
We can find another way to win.

39:38.666 --> 39:42.290
A way that will protect the innocent rather
than treating their lives like nothing!

39:42.750 --> 39:44.457
No such method exists.

39:44.625 --> 39:45.957
I’ve heard enough from you!

39:46.291 --> 39:47.790
I’ll negotiate with the enemy.

39:48.000 --> 39:49.000
It won't work.

39:51.250 --> 39:53.749
Squire, what did you just say?

39:57.041 --> 40:00.665
It won't work, and more people will die.

40:02.958 --> 40:05.624
You must sacrifice the one to save the many

40:05.958 --> 40:07.207
The Sorcerer King is correct.

40:07.375 --> 40:08.874
It's the only choice we have

40:09.083 --> 40:10.915
There is no justice in that.

40:11.666 --> 40:12.915
So what then?

40:13.875 --> 40:14.875
We lose?

40:15.223 --> 40:16.223
Is that Just?

40:16.458 --> 40:18.249
Please listen to Miss Baraja.

40:19.666 --> 40:20.707
That's enough!

40:24.333 --> 40:25.999
You've made your position clear.

40:26.541 --> 40:28.290
I believe it’s essential to take this city.

40:28.791 --> 40:31.165
Arguing over justification
will not serve that goal.

40:32.291 --> 40:33.291
Very well

40:33.625 --> 40:35.332
I shall tip the scales myself.

40:36.333 --> 40:37.832
You're sure about this?

40:38.750 --> 40:44.332
Every victory requires some sacrifice, but the
cost will be less if I step forward in your stead.

40:45.166 --> 40:49.124
Leave the Bafolk to me, and I believe
you will be satisfied with the results.

40:49.666 --> 40:51.874
But people will be killed?

40:52.833 --> 40:55.374
Unfortunately so, Grandmaster Custodio.

40:57.333 --> 40:58.333
Humans!

40:58.416 --> 40:59.915
This is your final warning!

41:00.666 --> 41:01.874
Surrender, or die!

41:01.875 --> 41:02.457
Third-tier magic Surrender, or die!

41:02.458 --> 41:03.458
Third-tier magic

41:04.041 --> 41:05.041
Fireball

41:11.750 --> 41:12.290
Your Majesty!

41:12.291 --> 41:13.291
Your Majesty!

41:13.916 --> 41:15.499
Forward, High Wraiths.

41:15.833 --> 41:17.540
Move in and await my orders.

41:20.916 --> 41:22.457
I'll go along with you.

41:22.958 --> 41:24.124
Are you certain?

41:24.125 --> 41:25.125
It's my duty.

41:26.541 --> 41:27.040
Hmm.

41:27.500 --> 41:30.207
In that case, you should
wear this around your neck.

41:31.166 --> 41:33.207
I don't know what it does, but thank you.

41:34.875 --> 41:38.499
I will release an aura that instills
fear in all those who come near me.

41:38.791 --> 41:43.790
The necklace will protect you, but tell the paladins that
they must prepare their own method to counteract the effects.

41:44.375 --> 41:45.874
The priest should cast Lion's Heart.

41:46.333 --> 41:48.665
I believe paladins can
use that Under Divine Flag.

41:49.125 --> 41:50.125
Is that correct?

41:51.208 --> 41:52.832
Yes, you’re quite knowledgeable.

41:57.541 --> 42:02.874
Miss Baraja, did you think I would use some sort
of unimaginable magic to save that young boy?

42:04.083 --> 42:05.083
Y-Yes.

42:06.041 --> 42:08.874
I could have done so if it was
the correct course of action.

42:09.541 --> 42:15.957
However, if we teach the enemy that hostages are effective,
they will continue to use prisoners inside the City as shields.

42:16.375 --> 42:19.374
Then, the paladins’ hesitation
will cause further harm.

42:19.375 --> 42:22.957
But I have demonstrated
that hostages are of no use.

42:23.125 --> 42:26.207
It seems cruel, but it will
prevent further sacrifices.

42:27.041 --> 42:28.665
Your judgment is correct. Your Majesty.

42:35.875 --> 42:37.165
Please, let me, Your Majesty!

42:37.791 --> 42:39.999
No. This was my decision.

42:52.291 --> 42:54.040
Bafolk will pay for this.

42:55.666 --> 43:00.499
I am the ruler of the Sorcerer
Kingdom, not the ruler of this country.

43:01.458 --> 43:08.124
If that boy was a citizen of my kingdom, then it
would have been my responsibility to protect his life.

43:08.125 --> 43:09.125
Of course.

43:09.750 --> 43:12.290
Your Majesty, you're like justice itself.

43:13.708 --> 43:15.415
Fear I don’t understand.

43:15.916 --> 43:16.499
I'm sorry.

43:16.916 --> 43:21.124
I mean, your reasoning is right,
and I believe that your actions are just.

43:21.125 --> 43:24.207
There is no justice or
injustice in my actions.

43:24.916 --> 43:28.207
I only wish for the peaceful
lives of myself and my children.

43:28.958 --> 43:30.040
There is nothing more.

43:30.541 --> 43:31.832
That is everything.

43:39.250 --> 43:40.290
Nolan...

43:40.291 --> 43:42.999
am the one who killed this child.

43:48.333 --> 43:49.665
A monster!

43:50.500 --> 43:51.749
You did this?

43:53.416 --> 43:55.374
To save all of your lives.

43:55.750 --> 43:56.790
To save us?

43:57.291 --> 43:59.124
It seems you have something to say.

43:59.875 --> 44:01.332
Then let me ask you this first.

44:01.791 --> 44:04.040
Why did you fail to protect your own child?

44:04.416 --> 44:05.790
I tried, of course.

44:06.625 --> 44:08.415
But he was taken away from me.

44:08.625 --> 44:10.457
Then why are you still alive?

44:10.458 --> 44:14.499
A person’s value is in
the eye of the beholder.

44:15.041 --> 44:18.624
But there is no one in the world who
you should value more than your own child.

44:19.416 --> 44:22.582
So I ask, why didn't you give
up your life to protect him?

44:23.375 --> 44:25.582
Why are you alive when he is dead?

44:26.791 --> 44:28.249
This was your failure.

44:28.916 --> 44:30.624
You have no right to blame others.

44:32.291 --> 44:35.207
You can say that only
because you’re strong.

44:35.208 --> 44:36.540
That's right.

44:37.000 --> 44:40.665
It was my strength that saved you,
and my strength that killed your son.

44:41.166 --> 44:45.707
If you say that you’re weak, then it is no
surprise that everything is taken from you.

44:46.500 --> 44:49.207
So that means you can
just do whatever you want?

44:51.041 --> 44:52.041
I do.

44:52.583 --> 44:55.290
If I am strong, then who will stop me?

44:55.916 --> 44:57.665
What I say will become right.

44:58.250 --> 45:00.249
That is the way of this world!

45:05.208 --> 45:08.082
I will forgive your words
because I take pity on you.

45:08.791 --> 45:10.082
I'll leave you with your child.

45:10.958 --> 45:12.207
You should mourn him.

45:26.041 --> 45:29.749
If I were weak, everything
would be taken from me as well.

45:30.666 --> 45:34.124
That is why I desire boundless strength..

45:34.125 --> 45:35.665
Your Majesty.

45:37.416 --> 45:39.832
It seems the enemy leader is up ahead.

45:40.708 --> 45:41.832
Will you come with me?

45:42.083 --> 45:43.083
Of course!

45:54.125 --> 45:55.290
Are they dead?

45:55.875 --> 45:57.374
This is the work of my undeads.

45:57.791 --> 46:00.749
I sent them ahead of us to
scatter fear amongst our foes.

46:05.416 --> 46:09.457
Is that him?

46:11.041 --> 46:12.041
Interesting.

46:12.250 --> 46:14.124
He has a number of magic items.

46:14.625 --> 46:16.374
I wonder which one countered the undeads.

46:18.875 --> 46:20.707
My name is Buser.

46:20.875 --> 46:23.290
They call me the Grand King Buser!

46:23.375 --> 46:24.375
He's a king?

46:24.458 --> 46:25.665
That can't be good.

46:26.333 --> 46:27.624
Your army is defeated.

46:28.250 --> 46:31.290
Do you wish to die, or do
you wish to submit to me?

46:31.916 --> 46:33.707
I shall allow you to choose.

46:37.500 --> 46:39.290
Bow my head to you?

46:40.000 --> 46:41.749
I am still a king!

46:42.416 --> 46:44.374
Bowing to that demon was enough!

46:46.000 --> 46:47.000
Fine then.

46:47.166 --> 46:48.415
I'll play with you a bit.

46:49.250 --> 46:52.999
By the way, goat, I see you're
armed to the teeth with magic items.

46:53.500 --> 46:57.790
But strangely, I don't sense any power
from those skulls dangling at your waist.

46:59.000 --> 46:59.499
What?

46:59.625 --> 47:00.874
You haven’t heard of fashion

47:01.041 --> 47:01.915
They're just bones!

47:01.916 --> 47:04.207
Very well, to each his own.

47:04.666 --> 47:06.040
Now let us begin.

47:06.833 --> 47:08.207
Create greater item

47:18.458 --> 47:20.582
All appraisal magic item.

47:24.000 --> 47:27.874
He defeated that terrifying
demi-human in a split second

47:28.250 --> 47:31.832
I knew the Sorcerer King
was amazing, but this is unreal!

47:57.458 --> 47:58.540
This is it.

48:00.000 --> 48:02.832
I sense an overwhelming
presence of fear in death.

48:10.750 --> 48:11.957
They're orcs!

48:15.750 --> 48:16.957
You’re an undead.

48:17.250 --> 48:18.250
What do you want?

48:18.750 --> 48:19.165
Nothing.

48:19.583 --> 48:21.374
I have simply come to set you free.

48:21.375 --> 48:22.790
Wait, your majesty!

48:23.333 --> 48:24.559
They’re demi-humans, aren't they?

48:24.583 --> 48:26.832
So these orcs must be
minions of Jaldabaoth!

48:27.333 --> 48:28.540
Really, Miss Baraja?

48:29.166 --> 48:30.540
Surely you don't believe that.

48:30.875 --> 48:31.999
Take a closer look.

48:33.500 --> 48:37.082
We have not attacked any
human country, I can assure you.

48:37.541 --> 48:38.541
What's your name?

48:38.791 --> 48:40.957
I am Dyel of the Gan Zu tribe.

48:41.500 --> 48:42.582
Servant to no one.

48:43.083 --> 48:48.124
If you are not at war like the rest of the
demi-humans, is that why you were imprisoned here?

48:48.708 --> 48:53.540
Not all of the demi-human tribes in the
Abilion Hills submitted to the demon willingly.

48:54.666 --> 48:56.957
Many were forced into
submission, you could say.

48:57.791 --> 49:03.332
We orcs resisted to the end, as punishment
Jaldabaoth brought us to this wretched place.

49:04.041 --> 49:05.041
What does that mean?

49:05.458 --> 49:06.458
What did he do?

49:10.166 --> 49:12.499
Honestly, dare I even imagine?

49:14.458 --> 49:17.207
It would seem I asked
an insensitive question.

49:18.291 --> 49:20.499
I will not demand that you join my army.

49:21.000 --> 49:22.832
I will free you to go where you please.

49:23.291 --> 49:24.749
But do you have somewhere in mind?

49:25.458 --> 49:29.707
We'll find the rest of our tribe, then go
someplace that Jaldabaoth can't reach.

49:30.208 --> 49:32.249
In that case, you should
come to my kingdom.

49:32.666 --> 49:33.666
We refuse

49:33.833 --> 49:35.874
Undead are the enemy of all living things.

49:36.000 --> 49:37.040
We wouldn't be safe.

49:37.125 --> 49:40.290
No, I assure you, there's
nothing terrifying about my country.

49:40.291 --> 49:41.291
He's telling the truth!

49:41.750 --> 49:45.082
He may be undead, but he is kind to
the living and protects all his subjects.

49:45.416 --> 49:47.999
He loves his children and
treats demi-humans equally.

49:48.250 --> 49:50.582
- He’s truly—
- Miss Baraja, that's enough!

49:50.833 --> 49:51.833
But your majesty!

49:52.500 --> 49:59.124
You may not believe us, but I swear on my honor as King
that you would never be treated like this under my rule.

49:59.708 --> 50:00.874
My subjects are my treasures.

50:01.500 --> 50:02.624
They must not be harmed.

50:03.333 --> 50:05.582
However, I will not
force you to submit to me.

50:06.083 --> 50:08.749
I can teleport you to your
village, if that’s what you want.

50:08.750 --> 50:10.249
We’re strangers.

50:10.666 --> 50:12.040
Why are you being so generous?

50:12.583 --> 50:14.082
I will defeat Jaldabaoth.

50:14.333 --> 50:15.999
To do so, I must weaken him.

50:16.666 --> 50:19.207
Spreading word of my kindness
will undermine his influence.

50:20.541 --> 50:25.874
If he rules over others with fear, as you said,
there may be demi-humans who wish to betray him.

50:26.416 --> 50:27.416
I understand.

50:27.750 --> 50:29.040
Then I wish you luck.

50:30.250 --> 50:33.624
Miss Baraja, stand outside
for a moment, please.

50:34.875 --> 50:35.875
All right.

50:39.041 --> 50:44.040
To his majesty, humans and demi-humans
are both worth protecting equally.

50:44.625 --> 50:46.790
This is the meaning of true kindness.

50:55.291 --> 50:56.499
Pardon the wait.

50:59.083 --> 51:01.790
Your majesty, so this is where you've been.

51:02.375 --> 51:03.375
Has something happened?

51:04.166 --> 51:04.707
Don’t worry.

51:04.916 --> 51:05.916
Good news this time.

51:06.333 --> 51:09.665
We found Sacred Princess
Calca's elder brother, here in the city.

51:16.250 --> 51:20.415
Prince Caspond, this is the man who has been
aiding our kingdom and liberated the city.

51:20.833 --> 51:23.499
He is known as the Sorcerer
King, Ainz Ooal Gown.

51:27.166 --> 51:28.457
It is truly a pleasure to meet you.

51:28.458 --> 51:29.476
It is truly a pleasure to meet you.

51:29.500 --> 51:30.915
Welcome, Sorcerer King.

51:31.458 --> 51:33.999
It's a pleasure to meet you
as well, Prince Caspond.

51:34.250 --> 51:35.665
I'm glad you’re safe.

51:36.189 --> 51:38.189
I apologize for meeting
in such a terrible state.

51:38.666 --> 51:41.249
A noble's elegance isn't
a matter of appearance.

51:46.375 --> 51:50.082
Thanks to your generous aid,
was set free from those demons.

51:51.250 --> 51:55.582
I would like to sincerely thank you for the
charity that you have shown to me and my people.

52:00.833 --> 52:03.665
I trust that the Sorcerer
King is gone for the night.

52:04.000 --> 52:05.707
Yes, we have prepared a room for him.

52:05.916 --> 52:07.316
He doesn’t know that we’re meeting.

52:08.375 --> 52:10.874
Good then.

52:12.958 --> 52:15.165
First of all, the Sacred Princess.

52:16.083 --> 52:18.874
I hear that my little-sister
Calca is currently missing.

52:19.291 --> 52:20.832
Have the demi-humans taken her?

52:21.500 --> 52:26.790
We have suggested such a possibility to the
Sorcerer King, but she is most likely dead.

52:27.000 --> 52:27.499
We have seen no evidence of that yet.

52:27.750 --> 52:29.101
We have seen no evidence of that yet.

52:29.125 --> 52:33.290
Even if that’s the case, we should be able to
resurrect her as long as we can find her body.

52:34.125 --> 52:37.790
My sister Kelart is alive out there
somewhere, and I know she could do it.

52:37.875 --> 52:39.540
We should continue
searching for her as well.

52:39.541 --> 52:42.582
I agree that recovering
Calca should be a priority.

52:43.583 --> 52:46.582
So, to that end, I will
make this city our base.

52:46.875 --> 52:49.582
From here, we'll wage war
against Jaldabaoth's army.

52:51.458 --> 52:52.458
That's far too reckless.

52:52.916 --> 52:57.415
We may have high walls, but if the enemy surrounds
us, it'll be over when we run out of food.

52:57.583 --> 52:59.665
You don't plan to go to
the Southern Territory?

53:00.208 --> 53:01.665
I will send a messenger instead.

53:02.291 --> 53:04.707
In truths those nobles won’t help us much.

53:04.708 --> 53:09.707
They all want the Sacred Seat, with means
they're hoping for news of my sister's death

53:10.333 --> 53:13.832
Regardless of our circumstances, I
cannot beg people like that for help.

53:15.208 --> 53:18.957
And as for the Sorcerer King,
he's here to-fight Jaldabaoth.

53:19.166 --> 53:22.582
Once he acquires his demon maids,
he will leave the kingdom correct?

53:23.083 --> 53:25.499
But that would create a problem for us.

53:25.833 --> 53:30.582
Even if their leader is killed plenty of
demi-humans we need His Majesty to call.

53:30.916 --> 53:34.124
I know, sir, but that's not the
arrangement we agreed upon, unfortunately.

53:34.375 --> 53:37.082
It would be easy for him to
thin their numbers with his magic.

53:37.250 --> 53:40.874
And the more demi-humans he
kills, the less our innocent citizens die.

53:41.625 --> 53:43.957
Tell me, which would you rather choose?

53:43.958 --> 53:48.332
An agreement that you made with an undead,
or the lives of our kingdom's people?

53:49.000 --> 53:50.999
The lives of our citizens, obviously!

53:52.791 --> 53:54.790
I’m so happy you see it my way.

53:56.291 --> 54:00.749
We know what he's capable of, so let's see
if we can put the Sorcerer King to work.

54:10.750 --> 54:11.874
Enemy attack!

54:14.250 --> 54:15.374
Enemy attack!

54:25.833 --> 54:27.540
Quite the force they've brought.

54:28.750 --> 54:30.832
We have about 10,000 soldiers.

54:31.333 --> 54:33.165
The enemy must have four times that.

54:33.458 --> 54:38.915
Our only hope for victory will be surviving till assistance
comes from the south, unless we can make the enemy retreat.

54:39.750 --> 54:41.874
Grand Master, so this is where you've been.

54:41.875 --> 54:43.874
Oh, it's you.

54:44.291 --> 54:45.540
Excellent timing, Gustav.

54:45.666 --> 54:47.290
I'd like to get your take on this, too.

54:47.958 --> 54:51.165
I'd love to discuss my ideas,
assuming I could come up with any.

54:51.791 --> 54:54.582
But there's a small complication
we need to deal with first.

54:54.708 --> 54:55.708
What is it?

54:55.791 --> 54:57.207
The citizens are troubled.

54:57.708 --> 55:02.665
They're worried about the upcoming battle, and they keep
asking if the Sorcerer King will be lending his aid.

55:03.000 --> 55:04.290
You know what he told us.

55:04.375 --> 55:08.124
If he doesn't conserve his magic power,
he won't be able to defeat Jaldabaoth.

55:08.250 --> 55:09.250
That's the deal.

55:09.541 --> 55:12.499
So until the Demon Lord
shows up, he won't lift a finger.

55:12.750 --> 55:15.749
The issue is that many people
saw him when he recaptured the city.

55:16.166 --> 55:20.665
They know he has abilities that far exceed the
Paladin’s, so they're looking to him for protection.

55:21.250 --> 55:26.082
If the citizens find out that their hero won’t be
standing with us, I fear that their morale will plummet.

55:26.291 --> 55:27.291
He's their hero?

55:27.333 --> 55:28.749
You're talking about an undead

55:28.833 --> 55:30.207
That doesn't matter to them!

55:30.583 --> 55:33.915
And besides, better they think
of him as a hero than a ruler.

55:34.375 --> 55:36.499
What if they want him as Sacred King?

55:36.500 --> 55:38.665
We still have a Sacred Princess, okay?

55:39.583 --> 55:40.665
She can’t be dead.

55:40.916 --> 55:43.957
The enemy must be holding her
hostage somewhere to keep an upper hand.

55:44.500 --> 55:45.500
Yes, my apologies.

55:46.166 --> 55:47.749
But it is a real concern.

55:48.000 --> 55:50.582
I fear the seat of the Sacred
Princess may be at risk.

55:50.875 --> 55:52.665
Princess Calca is a beloved ruler!

55:53.000 --> 55:54.540
Do you think his concerns are valid?

55:54.791 --> 55:59.332
Well, since we're Paladins, of course we
don’t consider the Sorcerer King to be a hero.

55:59.708 --> 56:04.499
But I do get the impression around town that the
citizens are starting to think of him that way.

56:04.500 --> 56:07.790
He exhibited so much power,
I can hardly blame them.

56:08.333 --> 56:09.374
Just what are you saying?

56:09.916 --> 56:13.040
Do you think it was a mistake to
bring the Sorcerer King here, Gustav?

56:13.375 --> 56:14.499
No, I wouldn't say that.

56:15.083 --> 56:17.499
It was the best decision you
could have made at the time.

56:18.375 --> 56:19.375
All right.

56:19.541 --> 56:20.915
Then what would you do now?

56:22.583 --> 56:26.582
Although the odds are not in our favor,
we must drive off the enemy on our own.

56:27.166 --> 56:31.124
If we don't, the fighting may
not end even if Jaldabaoth dies.

56:31.500 --> 56:33.624
We must protect our own kingdom.

56:40.791 --> 56:41.915
Why are we waiting?

56:43.375 --> 56:45.707
We've been sitting here for three days.

56:47.416 --> 56:50.082
I heard that city was
held by Grand King Baser.

56:50.250 --> 56:51.250
Is that the issue?

56:51.916 --> 56:54.332
Are you afraid of the enemy who killed him?

56:54.541 --> 56:56.624
They must be quite formidable indeed.

56:57.166 --> 57:00.124
Vijar, no need for you to get so worked up.

57:00.208 --> 57:01.540
You're such a child.

57:01.708 --> 57:04.249
Why not learn a bit of
patience before you mouth off?

57:04.583 --> 57:07.124
If we wait much longer,
you'll die of old age.

57:09.291 --> 57:11.207
That's enough from the both of you.

57:13.250 --> 57:15.207
We can’t have any dissent in our ranks.

57:15.500 --> 57:18.582
Would have to report the matter
to Lord Jaldabaoth if we did.

57:19.833 --> 57:23.415
As for the reason why
we haven't attacked yet...

57:23.416 --> 57:29.499
Lord Jaldabaoth ordered us to move our forces into place,
but to pause a few days so that the humans could watch us.

57:30.083 --> 57:32.624
He wanted their fear to fester and grow.

57:32.916 --> 57:34.082
I can't complain.

57:34.333 --> 57:35.332
That's quite clever.

57:35.333 --> 57:39.124
Now keep in mind, he didn't
designate an exact amount of time.

57:39.625 --> 57:41.707
So I say we attack the day after tomorrow.

57:42.500 --> 57:44.082
There was one additional order.

57:44.333 --> 57:45.582
He said it's very important.

57:46.250 --> 57:50.040
We need to leave a few humans alive
and allow them to escape from the city.

57:50.041 --> 57:50.415
We need to leave a few humans alive
and allow them to escape from the city.

57:50.708 --> 57:51.708
Very well.

57:52.166 --> 57:54.999
And that means we can
massacre the rest of them, yes?

57:55.333 --> 57:56.665
If you so please.

57:57.208 --> 58:00.915
Now, spend the next two
days replenishing your strength.

58:12.416 --> 58:14.040
Squire Neia Baraja here.

58:14.666 --> 58:15.707
You may enter.

58:21.541 --> 58:26.957
Your Majesty, I’ve been informed I’m to be deployed to
the front lines as a member of the Sacred Paladin Order.

58:29.333 --> 58:32.499
Therefore, I will be unable to
continue my duty as your attendant.

58:33.000 --> 58:35.499
I wanted to offer an
apology before I set off.

58:36.250 --> 58:38.915
I have used my magic several times already.

58:39.541 --> 58:42.207
Jaldabaoth may be aiming to
whittle it away with his forces.

58:42.208 --> 58:46.749
If he does not appear in this battle,
do not expect me to come to your aid.

58:47.500 --> 58:48.540
Yes, I understand.

58:49.458 --> 58:55.749
Even so, it is my duty as part of this kingdom to
protect as many innocent people as I possibly can.

58:56.333 --> 59:00.749
Those in pain and those who cannot
protect themselves must be cared for.

59:04.875 --> 59:07.290
I like that look in your eyes.

59:09.791 --> 59:13.999
And so, Squire Baraja, I
will lend you a few items.

59:17.333 --> 59:17.790
What?

59:18.000 --> 59:19.000
No, wait!

59:19.416 --> 59:20.999
You've already lent me this bow!

59:21.166 --> 59:24.249
I wondered if it was even appropriate
for me to use it in this battle.

59:24.416 --> 59:26.999
I only accepted it so I
could better serve you.

59:27.166 --> 59:30.790
This is the armor of the demi-human
king I defeated a few days ago.

59:31.250 --> 59:32.957
I'm certain it will keep you safe.

59:33.708 --> 59:36.165
And this is known as a visor mirror shade.

59:36.166 --> 59:39.207
- It helps to keep your vision clear, but it’s also—
- Your Majesty!

59:40.041 --> 59:44.290
I appreciate it, but I can't
possibly borrow all these!

59:45.083 --> 59:46.415
Then why not?

59:49.166 --> 59:51.499
How about a promise in exchange?

59:52.125 --> 59:55.707
When they're no longer needed,
you must come and return them to me.

01:00:04.833 --> 01:00:06.874
Thank you very much.

01:00:07.416 --> 01:00:12.082
I hope, I mean, I’ll definitely
survive and return these.

01:00:26.291 --> 01:00:27.291
It’s over!

01:00:27.333 --> 01:00:29.165
There’s no way we can win against that

01:00:30.125 --> 01:00:34.999
- If the Sorcerer King came and thinned their numbers, maybe we could—
- His Majesty isn't coming.

01:00:35.291 --> 01:00:37.165
He will not be taking part in this battle.

01:00:38.083 --> 01:00:40.540
Wait, aren’t you the
Sorcerer King’s attendant?

01:00:40.916 --> 01:00:42.832
Or, I mean, you were, at least.

01:00:43.458 --> 01:00:44.790
Yes, that's me.

01:00:45.000 --> 01:00:47.290
Then do you know why he won’t help us?

01:00:48.041 --> 01:00:51.457
His majesty needs to conserve his magic
power for the fight against Jaldabaoth.

01:00:51.750 --> 01:00:53.707
He's the only one who can kill that demon.

01:00:54.375 --> 01:00:54.915
That's all.

01:00:55.291 --> 01:00:57.290
So we must make do on our own today.

01:00:58.500 --> 01:00:59.582
We're outnumbered.

01:00:59.875 --> 01:01:01.374
They’ll tear right through us.

01:01:01.791 --> 01:01:03.374
Are you ordering us to die?

01:01:06.750 --> 01:01:07.874
What do you mean?

01:01:08.625 --> 01:01:10.540
This is our kingdom to protect.

01:01:12.541 --> 01:01:14.707
In the end, this is on our shoulders.

01:01:15.125 --> 01:01:16.125
It's our duty.

01:01:16.750 --> 01:01:17.999
And the Sorcerer King?

01:01:18.125 --> 01:01:19.707
He's not even from this place.

01:01:20.041 --> 01:01:21.374
He’s been generous enough.

01:01:21.458 --> 01:01:24.624
We can’t use our weakness
as an excuse to rely on him.

01:01:26.000 --> 01:01:28.249
It’s our kingdom and our war.

01:01:28.708 --> 01:01:30.749
It's our people that we must protect.

01:01:31.500 --> 01:01:34.624
So I’ll fight because that is justice.

01:01:36.208 --> 01:01:37.999
The demi-humans are strong.

01:01:38.208 --> 01:01:39.415
We're not even knights.

01:01:39.666 --> 01:01:40.874
We don't stand a chance.

01:01:44.250 --> 01:01:49.499
But that doesn't change the fact that
someone has to protect my wife and child.

01:01:50.500 --> 01:01:51.500
Huh?

01:01:51.750 --> 01:01:52.750
So I'll fight.

01:01:53.583 --> 01:01:54.583
I have to.

01:01:55.500 --> 01:01:56.500
Good.

01:01:56.791 --> 01:01:58.457
And I’ll fight with you.

01:02:20.041 --> 01:02:21.249
Don't be afraid.

01:02:21.750 --> 01:02:23.624
Under divine flag!

01:02:30.048 --> 01:02:32.048
The enemy's arrows won't rain down forever.

01:02:32.833 --> 01:02:33.833
Stay strong!

01:03:14.333 --> 01:03:16.457
Even with this, they're still too far away.

01:03:17.708 --> 01:03:18.499
It's coming!

01:03:18.708 --> 01:03:19.249
Pull back!

01:03:19.416 --> 01:03:20.416
Hurry

01:04:04.333 --> 01:04:05.915
We have to fight!

01:04:05.916 --> 01:04:07.249
If you have a bow, then shoot!

01:04:07.375 --> 01:04:09.249
And if you don't, then throw rocks!

01:04:09.416 --> 01:04:10.874
We just aren't strong enough.

01:04:11.708 --> 01:04:15.582
I know it hurts, but we don't have
the power to save those children!

01:04:21.000 --> 01:04:22.000
Ugh!

01:04:22.250 --> 01:04:23.457
Stop holding back!

01:04:23.583 --> 01:04:25.082
Attack them while you still can!

01:04:25.291 --> 01:04:26.790
We can’t protect those children!

01:04:26.958 --> 01:04:27.958
She's right!

01:04:28.208 --> 01:04:29.499
I know you.

01:04:29.541 --> 01:04:33.999
If they get past those walls, the women and
children here will suffer a fate worse than death

01:04:34.166 --> 01:04:36.457
You have to do it for your families!

01:04:36.750 --> 01:04:38.124
We've got no choice!

01:04:38.448 --> 01:04:38.984
Attack!

01:04:39.208 --> 01:04:40.582
Bring more stones!

01:04:59.625 --> 01:05:01.332
Oh, no!

01:05:05.750 --> 01:05:06.750
I'm okay.

01:05:07.583 --> 01:05:08.999
This must be his power!

01:05:10.333 --> 01:05:12.540
Tell the priest we need support.

01:05:14.541 --> 01:05:16.999
Stab them with your spears
while they're climbing up!

01:05:31.833 --> 01:05:32.499
Ready shields!

01:05:32.500 --> 01:05:33.040
Ready shields!

01:05:33.333 --> 01:05:34.540
First line, drop them

01:05:35.041 --> 01:05:36.041
Lets go!

01:05:37.833 --> 01:05:39.707
Second line, into position!

01:05:41.500 --> 01:05:43.749
Third line, spears forward!

01:05:44.916 --> 01:05:45.374
Fourth line, it's your turn

01:05:45.375 --> 01:05:46.707
Fourth line, it's your turn.

01:05:47.000 --> 01:05:48.457
Spears forward now

01:05:50.958 --> 01:05:54.165
Paladins, protect against
fear before we face the enemy!

01:05:54.708 --> 01:05:56.332
Under divine flag!

01:05:58.208 --> 01:05:58.957
This is it?

01:05:58.958 --> 01:05:59.540
This is it.

01:05:59.666 --> 01:06:00.165
All forces ready.

01:06:00.166 --> 01:06:01.166
All forces ready?

01:06:01.750 --> 01:06:03.249
Open the gates!

01:06:07.583 --> 01:06:09.915
You're not worth the dirt you stand on

01:06:10.083 --> 01:06:14.374
Your insect-ridden hides are so filthy,
they're not even suited to wipe my ass!

01:06:18.291 --> 01:06:19.832
Spears, pull!

01:06:21.125 --> 01:06:22.707
Spears, stab!

01:06:23.666 --> 01:06:25.707
Now, firebomb!

01:06:59.666 --> 01:07:02.790
I can't fight three of their
generals at the same time.

01:07:04.791 --> 01:07:05.791
Paladin Sabicus!

01:07:06.083 --> 01:07:07.083
Paladin Esteban!

01:07:07.500 --> 01:07:08.500
Yes, ma'am!

01:07:09.500 --> 01:07:10.500
They're strong.

01:07:10.833 --> 01:07:12.915
I need you to hold two
of them back for now.

01:07:13.125 --> 01:07:14.999
In the meantime, I'll kill the third one.

01:07:15.250 --> 01:07:16.250
Leave it to us!

01:07:16.458 --> 01:07:18.165
I’ll fight to my last breath!

01:07:18.583 --> 01:07:21.290
I’m fine facing all of
you at once, if you prefer.

01:07:22.041 --> 01:07:24.749
Do you think I would deny myself
the pleasure of sending you to hell?

01:07:24.750 --> 01:07:25.499
Do you think I would deny, myself
the pleasure of sending you to hell?

01:07:25.625 --> 01:07:26.749
Not on my life!

01:07:28.166 --> 01:07:30.415
She's a fighter just like you, Vijar.

01:07:30.750 --> 01:07:33.540
We'll let her give you that
fight you’re so hungry for.

01:07:35.375 --> 01:07:36.375
Impressive, human.

01:07:36.541 --> 01:07:37.999
That's a fine sword you've got.

01:07:38.541 --> 01:07:40.665
Tell me your name before you die.

01:07:41.250 --> 01:07:43.165
I'm Remedios Custodio.

01:07:44.250 --> 01:07:45.457
Well, how fortunate!

01:07:45.875 --> 01:07:48.755
You're hailed as the strongest paladin
in the whole kingdom, aren’t you?

01:07:50.083 --> 01:07:52.290
All that I seek is glory.

01:07:52.791 --> 01:07:54.290
I'm Vijar Rajandala.

01:07:54.791 --> 01:07:56.374
I'll take your head, human.

01:07:56.750 --> 01:08:00.124
After doing so, I will inherit the
title of Demon Claw at long last!

01:08:00.125 --> 01:08:01.790
That’s enough out of you!

01:08:11.375 --> 01:08:12.790
Strong strike!

01:08:13.333 --> 01:08:14.333
Fortress

01:08:16.291 --> 01:08:17.540
Power claw!

01:08:17.916 --> 01:08:19.457
Strong strike again!

01:08:24.000 --> 01:08:25.207
Mine's already dead.

01:08:25.333 --> 01:08:26.333
Oh no.

01:08:27.083 --> 01:08:28.999
Mine didn't put up much of a fight.

01:08:29.208 --> 01:08:31.082
Who's the slow one now, boy?

01:08:31.333 --> 01:08:32.790
Shall I lend a hand

01:08:33.083 --> 01:08:34.290
I'm here for glory.

01:08:34.583 --> 01:08:35.957
Why would I want help?

01:08:36.208 --> 01:08:39.124
It would seem we're free to do
as we please, Madam Nasrene.

01:08:39.250 --> 01:08:42.915
Perhaps we should break through that line
of shields and head further into the city.

01:08:42.916 --> 01:08:44.040
Like hell you will!

01:08:45.291 --> 01:08:46.582
Not so fast!

01:08:47.000 --> 01:08:49.207
How dare you take a back on our duel!

01:08:51.375 --> 01:08:52.375
Hold shield

01:08:52.625 --> 01:08:53.625
Maintain your position!

01:08:55.375 --> 01:08:57.874
I only get one of these, but here goes!

01:09:00.250 --> 01:09:02.249
Extreme holy strike!

01:09:08.583 --> 01:09:10.249
What the hell?

01:09:10.583 --> 01:09:11.707
Why didn't it work?

01:09:12.750 --> 01:09:16.499
That certainly looked impressive,
but it hardly stung at all.

01:09:17.000 --> 01:09:18.290
Was it just to frighten me?

01:09:19.250 --> 01:09:22.124
My holy light strikes
down evil without fail.

01:09:22.458 --> 01:09:27.290
After all that suffering you put us through, after
starting this damned war, you're still not evil!

01:09:28.458 --> 01:09:31.665
If it's any consolation, it did look nice.

01:09:32.000 --> 01:09:33.457
Why, it nearly blinded me.

01:09:34.875 --> 01:09:36.124
Fine work, human.

01:09:37.208 --> 01:09:41.040
Now they'll tell tales of how I survived
your greatest attack without flinching.

01:09:41.541 --> 01:09:44.957
Since you've played your part so well,
if you surrender, I'll kill you quickly..

01:09:45.250 --> 01:09:52.790
You have your fun, Vijar, but we can’t all afford to waste our time on
one woman, so we’re going to continue conquering the city without you.

01:09:55.375 --> 01:09:56.374
You protect the people, I'll fight alone.

01:09:56.375 --> 01:09:58.124
You protect the people, I'll fight alone.

01:09:58.291 --> 01:10:01.582
These are my people, and I
have swore to keep them safe.

01:10:02.708 --> 01:10:05.082
Pay her no mind, Madame Nasrene.

01:10:05.291 --> 01:10:09.082
I believe you have just the spell to
clean up those weaklings behind her.

01:10:09.458 --> 01:10:10.499
Indeed I do.

01:10:15.458 --> 01:10:16.624
Showdown declaration

01:10:18.875 --> 01:10:20.332
I can't move.

01:10:20.333 --> 01:10:22.540
As long as you fight me, you'll be fine.

01:10:22.791 --> 01:10:24.374
You will give me my due.

01:10:26.541 --> 01:10:27.541
Fireball!

01:10:31.250 --> 01:10:32.624
Wall of Skeleton!

01:10:38.250 --> 01:10:40.874
I believe there's a
lesson to be learned here.

01:10:41.166 --> 01:10:44.207
But three generals against
one just isn't very sporting.

01:10:44.500 --> 01:10:46.332
Who is that, an undead?

01:10:46.750 --> 01:10:48.040
So it would appear.

01:10:48.041 --> 01:10:51.415
My, I believe that's an elder lich.

01:10:51.500 --> 01:10:52.540
The Sorcerer King!

01:10:52.750 --> 01:10:53.624
He'll save us!

01:10:53.666 --> 01:10:55.165
Your Majesty, please

01:10:55.291 --> 01:10:56.957
We’re going to die!

01:10:58.875 --> 01:11:00.874
What do you think you're doing here?

01:11:01.750 --> 01:11:04.540
I believe that should be rather obvious.

01:11:09.625 --> 01:11:11.874
I came to save your lives.

01:11:12.458 --> 01:11:13.458
Is that so?

01:11:13.791 --> 01:11:14.999
Then I'll leave this to you.

01:11:16.125 --> 01:11:18.415
The Sorcerer King
will handle the front line!

01:11:18.875 --> 01:11:21.999
We will act as reinforcements
for whoever needs assistance.

01:11:22.791 --> 01:11:24.582
All soldiers, follow after me!

01:11:29.791 --> 01:11:33.415
Never in my life have I been
treated with such blatant disrespect.

01:11:34.375 --> 01:11:39.290
I thought it would be useful to have the Grandmaster
of the Paladins owe me a favor, but she's so rude!

01:11:39.625 --> 01:11:41.374
She doesn't appreciate me at all!

01:11:41.375 --> 01:11:44.374
Why would an undead come
to the rescue of humans?

01:11:45.000 --> 01:11:47.415
Are you being controlled
by a necromancer, perhaps?

01:11:47.833 --> 01:11:50.832
That woman doesn't hold you
in very high regard, does she?

01:11:51.583 --> 01:11:53.207
She left you here to die!

01:11:53.458 --> 01:11:54.458
Silence!

01:12:00.125 --> 01:12:01.290
What did you do?

01:12:01.375 --> 01:12:03.582
I demanded silence, if I recall.

01:12:08.375 --> 01:12:09.457
What did he..

01:12:13.791 --> 01:12:14.791
I miscalculated.

01:12:16.916 --> 01:12:18.457
Kill the demi-humans!

01:12:30.083 --> 01:12:35.124
If I’d known it would turn out this way, I would
have focused my efforts on Miss Baraja instead.

01:12:48.250 --> 01:12:53.374
Heed my words, for I am Jajan, and
am taking their commander's|head!

01:12:56.583 --> 01:12:59.999
Neia Baraja has slain Jajan of the Lagon!

01:13:07.500 --> 01:13:09.957
Be careful when
approaching that human girl.

01:13:11.250 --> 01:13:13.457
She's wearing the Grand King's armor!

01:13:13.875 --> 01:13:15.832
So was she the one who killed Buser?

01:13:18.416 --> 01:13:20.915
Her eyes have a wicked glare

01:13:25.833 --> 01:13:27.874
Looks like she's hungry for blood!

01:13:28.166 --> 01:13:30.499
And that bow is brimming with power!

01:13:37.208 --> 01:13:38.665
The Mad-Eye Archer!

01:13:39.416 --> 01:13:40.416
Who is she?

01:13:41.708 --> 01:13:42.415
Miss Ba raja, this area is done for.

01:13:42.416 --> 01:13:43.816
Miss Baraja, this area is done for.

01:13:45.125 --> 01:13:46.415
I can’t do that

01:13:47.750 --> 01:13:49.874
I have to return this weapon.

01:13:50.291 --> 01:13:55.582
But if I'm seen fleeing after receiving such a
powerful gift, it will reflect poorly on His Majesty.

01:13:56.500 --> 01:13:57.749
I must stand firm.

01:13:58.583 --> 01:14:00.082
Like hell I'd run

01:14:13.666 --> 01:14:14.874
I'm scared.

01:14:14.875 --> 01:14:16.415
She's faltering!

01:14:16.750 --> 01:14:17.790
Finish her off!

01:14:18.875 --> 01:14:20.624
Attack from all sides!

01:14:23.875 --> 01:14:25.957
This is it...

01:14:25.958 --> 01:14:27.957
I'm dead...

01:14:28.833 --> 01:14:30.249
Dad..

01:14:30.250 --> 01:14:31.250
Mom...

01:14:32.250 --> 01:14:33.874
Your Majesty...

01:14:45.708 --> 01:14:48.665
That was a close one.

01:14:50.500 --> 01:14:51.582
Your..

01:14:51.583 --> 01:14:52.624
Majesty

01:14:55.041 --> 01:14:58.207
Miss Baraja, rest and let me help you.

01:14:58.916 --> 01:14:59.916
You shouldn't move.

01:15:13.291 --> 01:15:15.290
No, that's a waste Your Majesty.

01:15:16.041 --> 01:15:17.041
I’ll be...

01:15:17.125 --> 01:15:18.125
fine..

01:15:19.791 --> 01:15:20.957
No, no

01:15:20.958 --> 01:15:23.540
I'll give you something to
recover your fatigue as well

01:15:26.083 --> 01:15:28.540
Forgive me for not reaching you sooner.

01:15:28.541 --> 01:15:31.582
Your Majesty, I'm worried, about you.

01:15:31.916 --> 01:15:33.540
What about fighting Jaldabaoth?

01:15:34.083 --> 01:15:36.290
What if he attacks and your magic is spent?

01:15:36.416 --> 01:15:37.416
You could die.

01:15:37.833 --> 01:15:39.457
I will face that when the time comes.

01:15:40.000 --> 01:15:41.707
In this case, I had no choice.

01:15:42.083 --> 01:15:43.540
I had to save you.

01:15:46.791 --> 01:15:48.040
I see now.

01:15:48.375 --> 01:15:49.832
I’m finally sure.

01:15:51.916 --> 01:15:53.832
About what justice means.

01:15:55.833 --> 01:15:58.499
It really was you, just like I thought.

01:15:59.458 --> 01:16:01.832
I'm afraid you might be a bit delirious.

01:16:02.791 --> 01:16:04.957
Justice takes strength and courage.

01:16:05.125 --> 01:16:07.415
Because if you're too
weak, you can't uphold it.

01:16:07.791 --> 01:16:09.999
But that doesn’t mean that
might alone makes right.

01:16:10.208 --> 01:16:12.499
It's what you do with that
strength that makes it just.

01:16:12.916 --> 01:16:13.957
Like helping others.

01:16:14.375 --> 01:16:18.082
Using your power to protect the weak,
even when it might bring harm to yourself.

01:16:18.541 --> 01:16:19.541
Like you did.

01:16:19.750 --> 01:16:21.999
That’s why I say you are justice itself-

01:16:24.823 --> 01:16:26.823
Your Magesty!

01:16:26.916 --> 01:16:28.415
We're all so grateful.

01:16:28.791 --> 01:16:31.957
Even though we're not your subjects,
you came here and saved our lives.

01:16:32.541 --> 01:16:33.874
It was a mere trifle.

01:16:34.500 --> 01:16:36.874
But I do have a favor to ask.

01:16:40.083 --> 01:16:45.457
If you would like to express your gratitude,
take her to a safe place until the battle is won.

01:16:48.083 --> 01:16:48.874
Thank you.

01:16:48.875 --> 01:16:56.040
Neia Baraja and everyone else in this
kingdom, you may leave the rest to me.

01:17:08.000 --> 01:17:09.957
Thank you, Your Majesty!

01:17:10.375 --> 01:17:11.375
You’re our hero!

01:17:12.000 --> 01:17:14.124
Hooray for the Sorcerer King!

01:17:26.666 --> 01:17:27.666
Hmph.

01:17:43.958 --> 01:17:44.958
Incredible.

01:17:45.083 --> 01:17:47.332
That's 40,000 demi-humans wiped out.

01:17:47.750 --> 01:17:50.290
This is a victory for the
history books, my lord.

01:17:50.583 --> 01:17:51.583
Don't you think?

01:17:51.875 --> 01:17:55.290
It is a victory, but I would
not call it ours to claim.

01:17:55.958 --> 01:17:59.582
The Sorcerer King claimed the
glory today, and he did it alone.

01:17:59.833 --> 01:18:00.833
You're wrong!

01:18:01.750 --> 01:18:03.832
All of us fought hard to save this city.

01:18:04.166 --> 01:18:05.582
Some lost their lives.

01:18:05.583 --> 01:18:08.457
That they did, and you
were there on the front line.

01:18:08.666 --> 01:18:09.957
You saw it firsthand.

01:18:10.500 --> 01:18:14.165
Our paladins and our citizens
fought and died for this land.

01:18:14.583 --> 01:18:16.749
No victory would be possible without them.

01:18:17.083 --> 01:18:18.415
That much I can accept.

01:18:18.958 --> 01:18:23.749
But frankly, despite their efforts, we would
have lost without then Sorcerer King’s aid.

01:18:23.958 --> 01:18:24.958
Am I wrong?

01:18:26.166 --> 01:18:29.832
Let me remind you, he only
joined us in the middle of the fight!

01:18:30.166 --> 01:18:32.874
Think about all of the brave
people who died before then!

01:18:32.875 --> 01:18:33.374
Our citizens, our paladins, our priests!

01:18:33.375 --> 01:18:35.999
Our citizens, our paladins, our priests!

01:18:36.416 --> 01:18:39.874
You’re saying they sacrificed
everything for no reason?!

01:18:41.000 --> 01:18:41.457
Grandmaster...

01:18:41.458 --> 01:18:42.915
You saw what he was doing!

01:18:43.250 --> 01:18:45.707
He was showing off just
to get people on his side!

01:18:46.166 --> 01:18:48.290
This war is nothing but
a game to him, I swear.

01:18:48.291 --> 01:18:50.149
This war is nothing but
a game to him, I swear.

01:18:50.173 --> 01:18:51.373
Wait, that's it.

01:18:52.197 --> 01:18:54.517
Jaldabaoth and the sorcerer
king must be working together.

01:18:55.916 --> 01:18:57.165
Look at what happened.

01:18:57.333 --> 01:18:59.665
He's the only one who
really benefited from this fight.

01:18:59.666 --> 01:19:00.082
He's the only one who
really benefited from this fight.

01:19:00.333 --> 01:19:01.333
It all maxes sense now!

01:19:01.541 --> 01:19:03.501
He weakens our kingdom,
but still plays the hero.

01:19:03.708 --> 01:19:05.165
Then in the end, he'll conquer us

01:19:05.250 --> 01:19:06.250
I'm sure of it!

01:19:06.333 --> 01:19:09.582
Grandmaster Custodio, this
has clearly taken a toll on you.

01:19:09.875 --> 01:19:10.957
Go and rest for now.

01:19:12.166 --> 01:19:13.166
This is an order.

01:19:21.083 --> 01:19:21.582
Get inside

01:19:21.906 --> 01:19:22.906
Hurry!

01:19:37.250 --> 01:19:38.915
Jaldabaoth!

01:19:39.291 --> 01:19:45.874
Forgive me if I'm interrupting your victory
celebration, but I'm afraid the battle's not over yet.

01:19:49.500 --> 01:19:51.082
You're in the way!

01:20:18.333 --> 01:20:19.333
Princess.

01:20:20.375 --> 01:20:20.999
Calca..

01:20:21.000 --> 01:20:26.499
My goodness, I suppose she wasn't a good
weapon after all, falling apart like that.

01:20:26.500 --> 01:20:32.999
Still, she would have remained in one piece at least if you
hadn't rushed in swinging your sword like some kind of savage.

01:20:40.416 --> 01:20:42.249
What a beautiful scream

01:20:42.250 --> 01:20:43.250
What a beautiful scream!

01:20:51.750 --> 01:20:57.957
Now then, you must be
the Great Sorcerer King.

01:20:58.333 --> 01:21:01.207
Or should I call you Your
Majesty Ainz Ooal Gown instead?

01:21:01.791 --> 01:21:02.999
Do pardon me.

01:21:03.416 --> 01:21:06.082
I'm a demon, but that's
no excuse to be rude.

01:21:06.583 --> 01:21:08.249
Let's dispense with the formalities.

01:21:09.083 --> 01:21:13.374
I assume you've come here to kill me, so
manners are hardly my priority at present.

01:21:14.333 --> 01:21:15.999
Yes, I want you dead.

01:21:16.250 --> 01:21:21.165
We could butcher each other's forces all day, but this
won't be settled till the two of us meet in battle.

01:21:21.166 --> 01:21:22.665
But I know you're strong.

01:21:23.166 --> 01:21:24.332
Stronger than even Momon.

01:21:24.625 --> 01:21:29.832
Which is why I’ve constructed a plan
to ensure my victory beyond all doubt.

01:21:31.333 --> 01:21:33.207
Those demon maids here too?

01:21:35.291 --> 01:21:36.374
Well, well.

01:21:36.541 --> 01:21:38.165
Your Majesty, do as you must.

01:21:38.291 --> 01:21:39.540
Don't worry about us.

01:21:41.916 --> 01:21:43.665
Consider it, you little human.

01:21:44.250 --> 01:21:47.832
Don't worry, you'll get your slow and
painful deaths once I kill your savior.

01:21:50.125 --> 01:21:51.415
Say your goodbyes.

01:21:51.500 --> 01:21:54.749
We shall wait for you at the
Clock Tower in the center of the city.

01:21:56.333 --> 01:21:59.832
I'm looking forward to this, Sorcerer King!

01:22:00.833 --> 01:22:03.415
Prince Casbond, I will buy you some time.

01:22:04.083 --> 01:22:07.915
You should order any people near the
center of the city to evacuate immediately.

01:22:08.708 --> 01:22:09.708
I understand.

01:22:10.166 --> 01:22:10.749
But wait!

01:22:11.125 --> 01:22:14.707
You've already used so much magic
to help us and you haven't rested at all!

01:22:14.875 --> 01:22:16.374
Are you going to be able to win

01:22:16.375 --> 01:22:16.749
It certainly will be dangerous, but I
fear I have no choice in the matter.

01:22:16.750 --> 01:22:21.290
It certainly will be dangerous, but
I fear I have no choice in the matter.

01:22:22.500 --> 01:22:23.290
What do you mean?

01:22:23.416 --> 01:22:25.665
The people of the
Sorcerer Kingdom need you.

01:22:27.583 --> 01:22:29.040
I made a promise as a king.

01:22:30.250 --> 01:22:30.957
I must keep it.

01:22:30.958 --> 01:22:31.958
I must keep it.

01:22:35.750 --> 01:22:41.624
Even if the circumstances aren't as I planned, the
demon has come to me and so I will destroy him.

01:22:42.083 --> 01:22:43.874
Then the maids will be mine

01:22:49.208 --> 01:22:50.208
Message.

01:22:50.375 --> 01:22:53.040
Hanzo, have you noticed anyone in the area?

01:22:53.916 --> 01:22:54.916
Pleiades?

01:22:55.208 --> 01:22:57.332
Oh yes, I know they’re here.

01:22:58.750 --> 01:23:02.290
No signs of any players or
world items this time either, huh?

01:23:02.708 --> 01:23:05.374
Was what happened to
Shalltear just a fluke or what?

01:23:06.000 --> 01:23:07.582
Never hurts to be extra careful.

01:23:08.166 --> 01:23:09.457
I’ll figure it out someday.

01:23:10.750 --> 01:23:12.082
Everything else is set.

01:23:12.541 --> 01:23:15.915
Now all I have to do is follow
Demiurge's plan, so it should be easy.

01:23:15.916 --> 01:23:19.707
Even if I screw something up,
I’ll just say I did it to test him.

01:23:21.083 --> 01:23:25.165
<i>This wouldn’t be an issue if Demiurge didn't
somehow get the impression that I was a genius.</i>

01:23:25.625 --> 01:23:29.957
<i>Half the instructions he gave me for this plan
were just, go with the flow, I trust your judgment.</i>

01:23:31.125 --> 01:23:34.085
<i>Hey now, Both of them, keep hitting
me with these completely insane ideas.</i>

01:23:34.416 --> 01:23:36.790
<i>Whoever heard of a king going
alone to aid another country?</i>

01:23:37.291 --> 01:23:38.540
<i>I'm out of my depth here!</i>

01:23:38.958 --> 01:23:40.707
<i>Think about these things for a sec!</i>

01:23:41.583 --> 01:23:43.332
<i>Okay, you got this, dude.</i>

01:23:43.958 --> 01:23:44.999
<i>Everything's fine.</i>

01:23:45.583 --> 01:23:48.124
<i>Just clear tills and it’s smooth sailing.</i>

01:23:53.958 --> 01:23:55.332
<i>This is just a plain
old evil lord of wrath.</i>

01:23:55.333 --> 01:23:56.726
<i>This is just a plain
old evil lord of wrath.</i>

01:23:56.750 --> 01:24:00.540
<i>Only difference is that Demiurge
summoned this one and its Level 84..</i>

01:24:01.416 --> 01:24:07.332
<i>Despite the fire, it's a pure warrior-type monster,
so that means powerful physical attacks and high HP.</i>

01:24:07.958 --> 01:24:10.124
I assume you've been informed of the plan?

01:24:10.833 --> 01:24:12.624
Yes, of course, my lord.

01:24:12.833 --> 01:24:14.540
Ready whenever you are.

01:24:15.541 --> 01:24:16.541
All right.

01:24:16.750 --> 01:24:22.374
Just to clarify, after the battle is won, you're
going to summon your demon to attack the city?

01:24:22.958 --> 01:24:24.332
That is correct, my lord.

01:24:25.083 --> 01:24:27.707
In that case, I have two requests.

01:24:28.416 --> 01:24:32.415
First, I'd like some support on a personal
project that hasn't been going well.

01:24:32.875 --> 01:24:33.875
Nothing too fancy.

01:24:34.583 --> 01:24:41.957
And secondly, I cannot let my combat skills grow dull, so I
want you to order your summoned demon to fight me seriously.

01:24:42.791 --> 01:24:44.582
But, my lord...

01:24:45.541 --> 01:24:46.582
We understand.

01:24:46.958 --> 01:24:47.499
Albedo!

01:24:47.875 --> 01:24:52.999
However, the evil lord of wrath will probably
not be enough to satisfy someone of your prowess.

01:24:53.625 --> 01:24:55.790
Why don't we hove the demon
maids join the battle as well?

01:24:55.791 --> 01:24:56.791
Maximize magic!

01:24:56.875 --> 01:24:57.875
Reality!

01:24:58.000 --> 01:24:59.207
Shizu here too?

01:25:00.916 --> 01:25:03.499
I fear I may accidentally
kill the Pleiades.

01:25:05.083 --> 01:25:08.332
Then we’ll use greater
doppelgangers to fight you in their stead.

01:25:08.583 --> 01:25:11.499
Their performance won’t
disappoint, I assure you.

01:25:12.500 --> 01:25:13.500
Hm?

01:25:29.625 --> 01:25:31.790
Why am I so weak?

01:25:36.083 --> 01:25:37.915
No, I said it myself.

01:25:38.125 --> 01:25:39.249
Power isn't enough.

01:25:39.458 --> 01:25:42.249
Even if I was as strong as a
demon lord, it wouldn't matter.

01:25:43.375 --> 01:25:45.249
But his majesty is different.

01:25:45.750 --> 01:25:48.165
He's the only one who embodies justice.

01:25:49.708 --> 01:25:50.874
Please, your majesty!

01:25:51.416 --> 01:25:52.999
You must triumph!

01:25:53.625 --> 01:25:54.625
You must!

01:26:37.666 --> 01:26:41.415
Your sorcerer kin is dead by my hand!

01:26:42.125 --> 01:26:42.957
You're lying!

01:26:42.958 --> 01:26:46.665
And I owe it all to you selfish humans.

01:26:49.666 --> 01:26:54.624
If the sorcerer king had been in proper form,
this victory surely would have eluded me.

01:26:55.416 --> 01:26:59.915
But he used his magic power to
help you worms again and again.

01:27:00.916 --> 01:27:05.332
He was a fool of a king undone by
his own misguided sense of kindness.

01:27:06.958 --> 01:27:12.582
But as you can see, he's dealt me
terrible blow, so I must depart and rest.

01:27:12.833 --> 01:27:18.040
I will spare your lives for now, but I
will return in time to strike you down.

01:27:18.791 --> 01:27:21.707
Until then, let your despair grow thick.

01:27:22.083 --> 01:27:23.249
I don't believe you!

01:27:23.416 --> 01:27:24.999
You’re nothing but a damn liar!

01:27:25.208 --> 01:27:27.665
You think I trust the words of a demon?

01:27:36.500 --> 01:27:39.582
That bow of yours is truly a fine weapon.

01:27:41.041 --> 01:27:44.415
It has been ages since
I've seen such workmanship.

01:27:44.958 --> 01:27:46.874
Why, you could have finished me off.

01:27:47.333 --> 01:27:48.915
A true demon slayer weapon.

01:27:49.333 --> 01:27:50.999
Tell me more of this bow.

01:27:51.000 --> 01:27:52.000
What is it made from?

01:27:52.458 --> 01:27:53.207
Go to hell!

01:27:53.208 --> 01:27:54.707
Hold on.

01:27:55.250 --> 01:27:59.207
Could it have been made with rune
technology thought to have been long lost?

01:28:00.166 --> 01:28:00.832
Enough!

01:28:01.041 --> 01:28:02.790
I won't say another word to you!

01:28:05.250 --> 01:28:08.207
Well, seems that’s the best I can do.

01:28:08.833 --> 01:28:10.207
Time for greater teleportation.

01:28:12.333 --> 01:28:13.790
Don't run away!

01:28:21.875 --> 01:28:23.165
Your Majesty.

01:28:43.958 --> 01:28:50.374
It’s already been three days since the disappearance
of His Majesty, and this is all I can accomplish.

01:28:51.333 --> 01:28:54.457
We need to form a search unit
and find him as soon as possible.

01:28:54.916 --> 01:28:57.082
We're wasting time when
there's none to spare.

01:28:59.708 --> 01:29:00.332
Why won’t Prince Caspond
do anything to help?

01:29:00.333 --> 01:29:02.415
Why won’t Prince Caspond
do anything to help?

01:29:05.041 --> 01:29:07.665
No, it's my fault for not
being strong enough.

01:29:08.250 --> 01:29:11.165
If I had the power, I could
go search for him myself.

01:29:15.375 --> 01:29:18.540
If justice takes strength,
then weakness must be evil.

01:29:18.750 --> 01:29:19.999
Squire Neia Baraja!

01:29:21.000 --> 01:29:23.249
Prince Caspond has requested your presence.

01:29:23.500 --> 01:29:25.082
All right, I’ll see him now.

01:29:25.458 --> 01:29:26.832
We can practice later, sorry.

01:29:27.041 --> 01:29:27.624
No problem.

01:29:27.958 --> 01:29:31.415
I don't think we'll be catching up with
you yet, but I do appreciate the lessons.

01:29:31.666 --> 01:29:34.749
We have to practice while we can for
when the demi-humans come back, right?

01:29:34.750 --> 01:29:35.750
That's right.

01:29:36.083 --> 01:29:39.415
We’ll continue our training and
grow stronger every single day.

01:29:40.000 --> 01:29:42.749
Weakness is a sin, so never give up.

01:29:43.500 --> 01:29:45.915
In regards to the Sorcerer King, well...

01:29:46.416 --> 01:29:48.540
You've decided to send a
search and rescue team?

01:29:48.791 --> 01:29:51.415
As I’ve told you many times
before, that's not possible.

01:29:51.875 --> 01:29:55.457
We think the Sorcerer King must have
landed in the Abileon Hills when he fell.

01:29:55.875 --> 01:29:57.082
It’s full of demi-humans.

01:29:57.250 --> 01:29:58.290
Completely unsafe.

01:29:58.958 --> 01:30:03.457
Unless we prepared a sizable force, we would just
be sending soldiers there to die senseless deaths.

01:30:03.458 --> 01:30:07.415
That aside, we should at least
search near the city in case he fell there.

01:30:07.500 --> 01:30:08.500
There’s no point.

01:30:09.166 --> 01:30:10.499
You saw it yourself.

01:30:10.958 --> 01:30:12.749
No one can survive a fall like that.

01:30:13.416 --> 01:30:15.332
The Sorcerer King's dead and gone.

01:30:15.583 --> 01:30:17.040
His Majesty is still alive!

01:30:17.333 --> 01:30:18.040
No, He's dead.

01:30:18.250 --> 01:30:20.874
You’re the only one holding
onto this ridiculous idea!

01:30:21.750 --> 01:30:24.624
If you two are done, I still
have something else to say.

01:30:25.541 --> 01:30:30.665
But before I start, we have a rather unusual
new ally that I need to introduce to you.

01:30:30.666 --> 01:30:32.249
I'll call her in now.

01:30:32.458 --> 01:30:33.874
Do not be alarmed.

01:30:37.750 --> 01:30:39.749
This is Emissary Beebeebee.

01:30:41.750 --> 01:30:42.290
A Zern?

01:30:42.666 --> 01:30:43.999
Yes, that's correct.

01:30:44.500 --> 01:30:47.290
Her people are currently trying
to rebel against Jaldabaoth.

01:30:48.166 --> 01:30:52.790
They’ve only been following his orders because a
member of their royal family has been taken hostage.

01:30:53.250 --> 01:30:58.082
We cooperated to ensure our king's safety, but when
we left the hills, the demons killed him anyway.

01:30:58.458 --> 01:31:00.999
Which means the prince
is our only remaining male.

01:31:01.333 --> 01:31:05.290
He's currently locked away in a tower in
a city about five days southwest of here.

01:31:05.291 --> 01:31:08.249
They want us to aid
them in a rescue operation.

01:31:09.041 --> 01:31:10.749
The Zern prince is being held in Kalinsha.

01:31:11.083 --> 01:31:13.457
It is an essential city
in our northern territory.

01:31:14.083 --> 01:31:19.040
So well form a small alliance, rescue the
Zern prince, then liberate Kalinsha together.

01:31:20.208 --> 01:31:24.582
If you grant us your cooperation, we have 3,000
soldiers who can help you take back the city.

01:31:25.208 --> 01:31:29.665
And after that, we should be able to send out
a rescue unit to search for the Sorcerer King.

01:31:30.166 --> 01:31:34.999
It's too dangerous to search the Abelion Hills on
our own, but we can do it with the help of the Zerns.

01:31:35.291 --> 01:31:38.999
What I’m getting at, Squire,
is that I want you on the job.

01:31:39.208 --> 01:31:41.124
Infiltrate the city and rescue the prince.

01:31:54.625 --> 01:31:57.124
So who will be joining me on this mission?

01:31:58.291 --> 01:32:00.832
Well, that is another surprise.

01:32:03.708 --> 01:32:09.540
After the Sorcerer King fought with Jaldabaoth, one of
the demon maid came to the city and surrendered to us.

01:32:10.208 --> 01:32:11.290
But why?

01:32:13.833 --> 01:32:19.290
Although the Sorcerer King did not triumph in battle, it
seems that he was able to seize control of one of the maids.

01:32:19.666 --> 01:32:21.540
She is now loyal to him instead.

01:32:50.041 --> 01:32:51.707
Neia Baraja here to see you.

01:32:51.958 --> 01:32:53.374
Could you please show yourself?

01:32:55.500 --> 01:32:57.457
Wow, what a great face.

01:32:58.791 --> 01:33:01.415
So you're Jaldabaoth’s
maid they're holding you here?

01:33:01.541 --> 01:33:01.999
Uh-huh.

01:33:02.416 --> 01:33:06.540
Though to be more accurate. I'd
say I'm actually Lord Ainz's maid now.

01:33:07.416 --> 01:33:09.082
You mean his majesty, right?

01:33:09.625 --> 01:33:11.749
Anyway, what do you want with me?

01:33:12.500 --> 01:33:13.500
We need to talk.

01:33:14.125 --> 01:33:16.624
I was hoping that you could
help me with the mission.

01:33:22.500 --> 01:33:23.500
Here, drink.

01:33:23.708 --> 01:33:24.708
What is that?

01:33:25.291 --> 01:33:26.291
It’s a chocolate drink.

01:33:27.500 --> 01:33:30.874
A bit high in calories though, like 2,000.

01:33:31.875 --> 01:33:33.707
But I wouldn't worry about it.

01:33:34.291 --> 01:33:36.832
Getting fat from eating
delicious things isn't bad.

01:33:37.333 --> 01:33:41.374
In fact, one of the Supreme Beings
even said you could call it a life goal.

01:33:42.541 --> 01:33:42.874
Well, guess I'll give it a try.

01:33:42.875 --> 01:33:44.207
Well, guess I'll give it a try.

01:33:46.875 --> 01:33:47.875
So sweet.

01:33:52.916 --> 01:33:54.374
Want another one?

01:33:56.333 --> 01:33:56.749
May I?

01:33:56.875 --> 01:33:57.875
It's really delicious.

01:34:06.333 --> 01:34:07.707
Thank you so much.

01:34:09.708 --> 01:34:10.874
Never mind that.

01:34:11.125 --> 01:34:13.082
I need to ask you some
questions, all right?

01:34:14.583 --> 01:34:18.249
Well, first, I know you're a demon
maid, but no one told me your name.

01:34:18.583 --> 01:34:20.124
Maybe you heard, but I'm Neia.

01:34:20.500 --> 01:34:23.749
Was serving as an attendant
for his majesty, the Sorcerer King.

01:34:24.208 --> 01:34:25.208
I know, yeah.

01:34:25.291 --> 01:34:27.624
I was warned about your scary-looking eyes.

01:34:28.583 --> 01:34:29.874
You can call me Shizu.

01:34:30.625 --> 01:34:31.625
What's the mission?

01:34:34.416 --> 01:34:35.790
All right, I understand.

01:34:36.375 --> 01:34:40.082
The two of us will sneak into the castle
and save the prince from that tower.

01:34:40.625 --> 01:34:44.957
When we're done, your army and
the Zerns will take back Kalinsha.

01:34:45.250 --> 01:34:45.665
Correct.

01:34:46.166 --> 01:34:47.832
Also, the Zerns gave me a warning.

01:34:48.125 --> 01:34:50.332
They said there may be a
great demon at the castle.

01:34:50.625 --> 01:34:52.749
We might run into it on
the way to the prince's room.

01:34:53.125 --> 01:34:54.457
Do you know anything about it?

01:34:55.250 --> 01:35:01.624
There are three, but lucky for us, they take turns watching
the city, so there shouldn't be more than one around.

01:35:02.666 --> 01:35:04.874
That's good, but how
strong are these things?

01:35:07.291 --> 01:35:09.957
Well, all right, then how strong
are they compared to you?

01:35:10.500 --> 01:35:11.500
Hard to say.

01:35:11.750 --> 01:35:13.707
I know they're weaker than Lord Ainz.

01:35:13.791 --> 01:35:15.082
Call him His Majesty.

01:35:16.500 --> 01:35:18.499
His Majesty the Sorcerer King.

01:35:18.875 --> 01:35:22.832
I think that Lord Ainz is a little too
casual especially coming from a maid.

01:35:22.916 --> 01:35:23.957
Just what do you mean?

01:35:24.083 --> 01:35:26.290
He told me I should call him that himself.

01:35:26.500 --> 01:35:27.790
I think it's just fine.

01:35:28.416 --> 01:35:34.332
He gave me specific permission
to use his name, so it's Lord Ainz.

01:35:34.541 --> 01:35:35.541
Understand me?

01:35:35.666 --> 01:35:36.290
Hold on!

01:35:36.500 --> 01:35:37.624
But you just met him.

01:35:37.750 --> 01:35:39.499
You're saying he's told you
to do that during the fight?

01:35:39.500 --> 01:35:41.249
I’m afraid you have to face the truth.

01:35:42.250 --> 01:35:45.499
I know this has come as a
great shock to you, but I’m special.

01:35:46.166 --> 01:35:46.790
It's all right.

01:35:47.000 --> 01:35:48.832
Not everyone can start out at the top.

01:35:49.500 --> 01:35:55.332
Someday, if you work hard and you keep the faith, I truly
believe that you can be part of the Lord Ainz Club with me.

01:35:56.000 --> 01:35:57.000
You have potential.

01:35:58.416 --> 01:35:58.832
Shizu...

01:35:58.833 --> 01:36:01.040
It's an expert's job to guide a trainee.

01:36:01.333 --> 01:36:02.915
I think we will make a good team.

01:36:03.500 --> 01:36:04.500
Well, thank you.

01:36:04.833 --> 01:36:05.957
That's good at least.

01:36:06.250 --> 01:36:12.290
I know that I just met you, but anyone who's able to
appreciate the greatness of Lord Ainz should be given mercy.

01:36:12.875 --> 01:36:16.749
Even though you're a demon and even though
you're a little bit confusing, I have to agree.

01:36:17.500 --> 01:36:20.540
Our mutual love of His
Majesty will see us through.

01:36:20.750 --> 01:36:21.999
I'm glad that I met you.

01:36:27.458 --> 01:36:31.082
You're a human, but those
bold eyes are very good.

01:36:31.458 --> 01:36:37.832
I admit when you first came here I thought it wouldn’t matter
if you died on the mission, but now I will protect you.

01:36:39.041 --> 01:36:41.957
Lord Ainz gave me one order
before the end of the battle.

01:36:42.208 --> 01:36:44.665
He told me to cooperate
with you and your allies.

01:36:45.166 --> 01:36:48.290
No dying, but I’ll do
anything else to help you out.

01:36:48.958 --> 01:36:49.958
Works for me.

01:36:50.458 --> 01:36:51.458
Good.

01:36:52.750 --> 01:36:53.999
What did you just do?

01:36:54.333 --> 01:36:55.332
What is this weird thing?

01:36:55.333 --> 01:36:58.082
I put these on cute things,
or on you in this case.

01:36:58.083 --> 01:37:00.540
Okay, but what is it and
why is it on my head?

01:37:00.916 --> 01:37:01.374
I know.

01:37:01.541 --> 01:37:02.999
You're like a little sister.

01:37:04.666 --> 01:37:05.666
Okay, fine.

01:37:08.500 --> 01:37:11.707
Now take it, but stick it
someplace you can see.

01:37:13.333 --> 01:37:14.333
Okay.

01:37:14.500 --> 01:37:15.790
Are we done talking?

01:37:16.416 --> 01:37:18.290
No, wait, one more thing

01:37:18.833 --> 01:37:21.874
Once we've rescued the prince,
I want to search for His Majesty.

01:37:22.333 --> 01:37:25.499
I mean we still need to find
out where His Majesty fell down.

01:37:25.583 --> 01:37:26.583
Sounds good to me.

01:37:26.750 --> 01:37:27.790
Yes, let's do that.

01:37:27.914 --> 01:37:28.914
Really?

01:37:29.000 --> 01:37:32.582
Thing is, we don't know if His
Majesty is all right or not yet.

01:37:32.875 --> 01:37:34.624
He might be stuck in enemy territory.

01:37:35.083 --> 01:37:38.290
I have faith that he’ll pull through
somehow, but I fear the worst.

01:37:38.416 --> 01:37:39.582
What are you talking about?

01:37:40.666 --> 01:37:41.666
He’s fine.

01:37:41.708 --> 01:37:42.708
He's not dead.

01:37:43.500 --> 01:37:46.957
The fact that Lord Ainz has
me under his control is proof.

01:37:51.041 --> 01:37:52.749
Why are you crying?

01:37:56.041 --> 01:37:59.707
I'm happy that he's still alive.

01:38:04.625 --> 01:38:06.582
Wow, it's a whole snot bridge.

01:38:06.875 --> 01:38:08.415
I’m kind of impressed.

01:38:11.083 --> 01:38:12.915
I'll wash it and give it back, okay?

01:38:13.166 --> 01:38:14.249
Really, I'm so sorry.

01:38:14.250 --> 01:38:15.749
This is embarrassing.

01:38:22.250 --> 01:38:23.665
Kalinsha is just up ahead.

01:38:36.250 --> 01:38:37.290
Stop there.

01:38:38.458 --> 01:38:39.832
We’re just bringing in rations.

01:38:44.083 --> 01:38:45.915
Are you satisfied yet?

01:39:22.166 --> 01:39:25.665
That was rough.

01:39:26.583 --> 01:39:28.165
You’ve got some meat in your hair.

01:39:28.689 --> 01:39:29.689
Hmm?

01:39:36.041 --> 01:39:37.099
Need a towel?

01:39:37.833 --> 01:39:40.749
I’m never hiding in a
barrel of raw meat again.

01:39:41.500 --> 01:39:44.749
Well, I mean, we'll have
to do it when we sneak out.

01:39:52.791 --> 01:39:54.082
That's so handy.

01:39:55.750 --> 01:39:56.874
Are you ready?

01:39:59.333 --> 01:40:03.040
The Zern Prince is being held
captive in a detached castle tower.

01:40:03.041 --> 01:40:07.999
We can only reach it by crossing the Sky Bridge,
which is connected to the building we're in now.

01:40:08.500 --> 01:40:13.624
Unfortunately, before we can make it to the bridge, we'll have
to get through a long passageway that has no places to hide.

01:40:14.166 --> 01:40:14.582
Understood.

01:40:15.083 --> 01:40:16.083
And after that?

01:40:16.375 --> 01:40:18.665
We'll enter a room where
some rope has been prepared.

01:40:19.125 --> 01:40:20.999
Then well rappel down to another floor.

01:40:48.625 --> 01:40:49.665
Thanks, Shizu.

01:40:51.166 --> 01:40:52.915
Neia, you’re way too slow.

01:41:02.583 --> 01:41:03.790
I'll take the right.

01:41:04.291 --> 01:41:05.374
Left one is yours.

01:41:12.750 --> 01:41:15.290
From here on out, it's a race against time.

01:41:18.583 --> 01:41:21.249
If I slip up, just ignore
me and keep going.

01:41:21.625 --> 01:41:23.749
The rescue mission is
more important than...

01:41:24.958 --> 01:41:25.958
Um...

01:41:26.166 --> 01:41:27.040
Wait here.

01:41:27.041 --> 01:41:29.165
I've got a trick that I can use.

01:41:48.875 --> 01:41:49.915
All clear.

01:41:50.250 --> 01:41:51.250
Are you ready to go?

01:41:52.791 --> 01:41:57.249
Can only use that full stealth
ability once a day, so let's be careful.

01:41:58.041 --> 01:41:59.041
Right, I understand.

01:42:12.583 --> 01:42:13.665
Probably a guard.

01:42:14.333 --> 01:42:15.874
Let's take it down immediately.

01:42:16.458 --> 01:42:17.458
I’m ready.

01:42:19.500 --> 01:42:21.207
Who the hell are you?

01:42:25.916 --> 01:42:27.832
We can't get past, what should we do?

01:42:27.875 --> 01:42:30.374
Our only option is to go on
the offensive at full speed.

01:42:30.500 --> 01:42:32.332
If we wait around, more guards will come.

01:42:32.333 --> 01:42:33.582
So let's charge straight in.

01:42:36.458 --> 01:42:40.040
How do humans make it to
this tower in the first place?

01:42:48.500 --> 01:42:51.082
I'm afraid projectiles don't work on me.

01:42:51.708 --> 01:42:55.124
No one can be invincible to
every kind of ranged attack.

01:42:55.541 --> 01:42:57.915
No one on this guy’s level, at least.

01:42:58.541 --> 01:42:59.874
It's some kind of trick.

01:43:00.041 --> 01:43:00.374
Yeah

01:43:00.666 --> 01:43:01.249
Try me!

01:43:01.416 --> 01:43:01.999
You'll see!

01:43:02.083 --> 01:43:03.083
Step away.

01:43:07.125 --> 01:43:08.582
Look at that!

01:43:08.708 --> 01:43:09.915
Just like I said!

01:43:10.125 --> 01:43:12.665
Your arrows won't work
on me, you dumb human!

01:43:13.000 --> 01:43:15.082
Now die, you fools!

01:43:17.708 --> 01:43:19.124
Come on, you little brat!

01:43:19.250 --> 01:43:20.250
Give it up already!

01:43:22.875 --> 01:43:24.624
Why are you aiming for her?

01:43:25.750 --> 01:43:29.374
You're attacking her even though
her arrows are useless against you.

01:43:29.666 --> 01:43:30.957
It doesn't make sense.

01:43:31.916 --> 01:43:34.124
She's in the way and I hate her face!

01:43:34.375 --> 01:43:35.832
I bet she can hurt you.

01:43:36.958 --> 01:43:38.457
You must have a limit.

01:43:39.958 --> 01:43:40.958
Now, Neia!

01:43:41.125 --> 01:43:41.790
I got it!

01:43:42.000 --> 01:43:43.000
I'll try!

01:43:47.083 --> 01:43:48.290
Seven times.

01:43:49.416 --> 01:43:50.540
That's the limit.

01:43:51.000 --> 01:43:54.790
He can resist ranged attacks
like he said, but only seven times.

01:43:55.791 --> 01:43:57.540
Is that seven in a day?

01:43:58.125 --> 01:43:59.125
Seven in an hour?

01:43:59.250 --> 01:44:00.250
Not sure.

01:44:01.541 --> 01:44:03.457
Doesn't matter much either way.

01:44:03.750 --> 01:44:04.750
You’re dead now.

01:44:05.041 --> 01:44:06.041
We'll finish you.

01:44:06.833 --> 01:44:09.040
The hell you will!

01:44:09.041 --> 01:44:10.540
Dark Cloud.

01:44:15.958 --> 01:44:17.915
He's gone around behind you.

01:44:19.166 --> 01:44:20.166
Neia, duck!

01:44:21.208 --> 01:44:22.499
Let's change it up.

01:44:22.875 --> 01:44:23.875
Full burst mode.

01:44:34.666 --> 01:44:37.832
That was really something.

01:44:38.583 --> 01:44:40.040
Are you okay, Neia?

01:44:40.083 --> 01:44:41.083
I’m fine.

01:44:41.291 --> 01:44:43.999
One of my arms hurts though,
so it's hard to shoot my bow.

01:44:44.000 --> 01:44:45.790
Do you have a healing potion on you?

01:44:45.916 --> 01:44:46.916
No, I don't.

01:44:47.125 --> 01:44:50.082
But we just have to rescue the
hostage now, so I should be all right.

01:44:51.166 --> 01:44:52.166
Then let's go.

01:44:55.958 --> 01:45:02.082
One of the items that his majesty gave me casts a healing
spell, but I only have enough magic power to use it once.

01:45:02.541 --> 01:45:05.165
My arm hurts, but I'd better
save it in case of an emergency.

01:45:07.166 --> 01:45:08.166
We're here.

01:45:08.333 --> 01:45:09.333
Ready.

01:45:13.666 --> 01:45:14.666
It’s empty.

01:45:25.875 --> 01:45:26.915
Don't shoot him

01:45:27.041 --> 01:45:28.415
You had the right room after all.

01:45:28.500 --> 01:45:29.500
This is the prince.

01:45:29.666 --> 01:45:30.666
This thing?

01:45:31.708 --> 01:45:32.708
Hello there.

01:45:32.833 --> 01:45:34.999
So, uh, you can speak, can't you, prince?

01:45:35.250 --> 01:45:36.250
Of course.

01:45:36.583 --> 01:45:37.707
But who are you?

01:45:37.916 --> 01:45:40.999
Assume you ladies weren't
sent here to be part of my meal.

01:45:41.541 --> 01:45:45.540
Actually, we're here to set you
free on behalf of another Zern.

01:45:45.583 --> 01:45:46.749
One of my emissaries?

01:45:47.583 --> 01:45:49.624
Uh, I just know her name is Beebeebee.

01:45:49.958 --> 01:45:50.958
Beebeebee, you say?

01:45:51.666 --> 01:45:57.707
Well, I appreciate the sentiment, but if I leave this
place, I will surely invoke Lord Jaldabaoth's wrath.

01:45:58.250 --> 01:46:02.665
That will put my people, and most
importantly, our king in terrible danger.

01:46:03.250 --> 01:46:09.874
I don't know all the details, but it seems that your king was
killed, which is why the Zerns went to rescue you at any cost.

01:46:09.875 --> 01:46:10.999
My father?

01:46:11.416 --> 01:46:12.416
It can’t be.

01:46:12.625 --> 01:46:14.540
The city will be liberated soon.

01:46:14.750 --> 01:46:16.832
The Zerns made an
alliance with our human army.

01:46:17.083 --> 01:46:19.999
When they hear that you're safe,
they'll make their move and attack.

01:46:20.625 --> 01:46:21.625
Very well.

01:46:22.666 --> 01:46:28.415
I know you are heroes who have risked your lives to
save me, but I'm afraid I must ask a shameless request.

01:46:28.750 --> 01:46:33.290
As a safety precaution, will you please act as if
you are taking me from this place against my will?

01:46:33.541 --> 01:46:35.707
You’re trying to protect
your people, aren't you?

01:46:35.833 --> 01:46:36.957
What a fine prince.

01:46:37.125 --> 01:46:39.415
If that's the case, consider
us your kidnappers.

01:46:40.583 --> 01:46:41.749
I am grateful.

01:46:42.625 --> 01:46:44.457
This isn't uncomfortable, is it?

01:46:44.791 --> 01:46:49.582
I'm fine here on your shoulder, but you smell
so nice that it whets my appetite a bit.

01:46:49.708 --> 01:46:51.415
Do the Zerns eat human flesh?

01:46:51.666 --> 01:46:54.832
No, we eat bodily fluids,
from the living or dead.

01:46:56.416 --> 01:46:58.999
Don’t munch on her or I’ll get real mad.

01:46:59.500 --> 01:47:03.457
Do you really think I'm voracious enough
to eat my own savior during our escape?

01:47:04.250 --> 01:47:05.415
I hope not.

01:47:05.625 --> 01:47:06.625
Let's go.

01:47:10.750 --> 01:47:12.915
I sense multiple people in this room.

01:47:12.916 --> 01:47:13.957
I’ll be ready.

01:47:17.250 --> 01:47:17.790
Don’t know who they are, but they’re Zerns.

01:47:18.166 --> 01:47:19.886
Don't know who they are, but they're Zerns.

01:47:19.958 --> 01:47:20.958
Is that good?

01:47:22.625 --> 01:47:23.790
Prince, you're safe!

01:47:24.125 --> 01:47:25.125
It's Beebeebee!

01:47:27.250 --> 01:47:29.415
I've been told that my father has passed.

01:47:29.958 --> 01:47:31.290
But what do you plan to do?

01:47:31.666 --> 01:47:34.665
If we run away, it will only set
us on the path to destruction.

01:47:35.083 --> 01:47:36.415
I worry too.

01:47:36.500 --> 01:47:37.500
It’s frightening.

01:47:37.666 --> 01:47:41.915
But we cannot stay with Jaldabaoth when
he only sees us as slaves and livestock.

01:47:41.916 --> 01:47:48.540
Even if he conquers this land, we will not find peace
judging by how he has mistreated dear Bubebebe already.

01:47:51.750 --> 01:47:54.290
Get here a bit faster next time.

01:47:57.750 --> 01:47:58.750
Not Bubebebe!

01:47:59.500 --> 01:48:03.874
Also, as we feared, one of Jaldabaoth's
demon aids is on site here at the castle.

01:48:04.083 --> 01:48:05.499
It's the one with two heads.

01:48:05.500 --> 01:48:06.999
A circlet, I see.

01:48:07.458 --> 01:48:10.624
It's a kind of demon that wears
the heads of two magic casters.

01:48:10.625 --> 01:48:12.249
Then it uses their spells.

01:48:12.958 --> 01:48:14.332
This is a good chance.

01:48:14.625 --> 01:48:15.749
We should kill it.

01:48:17.125 --> 01:48:17.499
I agree.

01:48:17.750 --> 01:48:19.499
Our future depends on your strength.

01:48:20.000 --> 01:48:22.082
If we've come this far,
then we must go all the way.

01:48:23.291 --> 01:48:24.291
Your Highness.

01:48:34.541 --> 01:48:35.541
No guards.

01:48:35.625 --> 01:48:36.625
It's all alone.

01:48:37.125 --> 01:48:38.125
Good, then.

01:48:38.291 --> 01:48:39.915
This will be our best chance to slay it.

01:48:40.291 --> 01:48:40.749
Let's go.

01:48:40.750 --> 01:48:41.750
Hm.

01:48:45.250 --> 01:48:46.582
A human?

01:48:47.416 --> 01:48:48.624
Yin Five Elements, Grand Fireball!

01:48:48.625 --> 01:48:49.892
Yin Five Elements, Grand Fireball!

01:48:49.916 --> 01:48:52.207
Yang Five Elements, Grand Fireball!

01:48:53.583 --> 01:48:54.707
As I thought.

01:48:54.875 --> 01:48:58.249
Is that the Zern Prince wrapped
around that human's back?

01:48:58.750 --> 01:49:02.124
Then I assume you’re not here
to offer them as a new prisoner.

01:49:05.708 --> 01:49:07.082
A betrayal.

01:49:07.750 --> 01:49:08.957
How interesting.

01:49:16.000 --> 01:49:18.040
Oh no, it’s her.

01:49:21.625 --> 01:49:24.499
High Priestess, Kelart Custodio.

01:49:26.833 --> 01:49:29.540
I didn’t expect this from you, Zerns.

01:49:29.833 --> 01:49:32.082
I thought we were getting along so well.

01:49:32.375 --> 01:49:35.249
Does this mean you don't
care what happens to your king?

01:49:35.375 --> 01:49:36.749
We know that you killed him!

01:49:37.041 --> 01:49:39.124
You can't control us
with your threats anymore!

01:49:39.958 --> 01:49:40.332
He’s dead.

01:49:40.333 --> 01:49:41.333
He's dead.

01:49:41.416 --> 01:49:42.749
I hadn’t heard that yet.

01:49:43.333 --> 01:49:44.999
Oh well, it doesn't matter.

01:49:45.458 --> 01:49:48.332
You probably killed him
because he got too full of himself.

01:49:48.791 --> 01:49:51.749
And now you’ll suffer the exact same fate.

01:49:51.958 --> 01:49:52.790
How dare you!

01:49:52.875 --> 01:49:55.332
I know you traitors can’t
defeat me on your own.

01:49:55.666 --> 01:49:57.874
Was that human supposed
to be your trump card?

01:49:58.000 --> 01:49:59.000
You'll find out!

01:49:59.375 --> 01:50:00.874
This discussion is over.

01:50:01.291 --> 01:50:03.082
Come forth, Shadow Demons!

01:50:04.208 --> 01:50:04.707
I

01:50:05.166 --> 01:50:08.415
Kill all the female Zerns,
but spare the prince.

01:50:08.833 --> 01:50:11.165
You’re going back to your room, boy.

01:50:12.541 --> 01:50:15.874
Human, there's no chance of winning
by siding with the Zerns.

01:50:16.375 --> 01:50:18.957
Do you have any friends or loved
ones who have been captured?

01:50:19.500 --> 01:50:21.999
Join me and I'll see that
their lives are spared.

01:50:23.000 --> 01:50:24.000
You mean that?

01:50:24.583 --> 01:50:26.999
You've come this far and now you betray us?

01:50:27.291 --> 01:50:27.749
Silence!

01:50:28.250 --> 01:50:30.540
You're not part of this conversation, worm.

01:50:31.625 --> 01:50:33.874
Tell me who you'd like to protect, human.

01:50:34.041 --> 01:50:35.874
Whose lives would you like to save?

01:50:36.500 --> 01:50:38.207
It’s all in your hands.

01:50:40.041 --> 01:50:40.499
What?

01:50:40.916 --> 01:50:41.582
It's your..

01:50:41.583 --> 01:50:42.749
No time to explain.

01:50:50.416 --> 01:50:52.790
Gene 5 Elements, Lightning Claw!

01:50:53.916 --> 01:50:56.249
Yang 5 Elements, Lightning Claw!

01:50:58.791 --> 01:51:00.082
Little pest.

01:51:00.791 --> 01:51:01.791
Shockwave

01:51:03.541 --> 01:51:05.540
Gene 1 Elements, Lightning Claw!

01:51:06.500 --> 01:51:08.624
Yang 5 Elements, Lightning Claw!

01:51:10.958 --> 01:51:12.582
Open wounds!

01:51:12.958 --> 01:51:14.249
That looks bad.

01:51:17.500 --> 01:51:18.790
Heavy, recover!

01:51:22.041 --> 01:51:23.124
I see.

01:51:25.583 --> 01:51:26.583
Shockwave!

01:51:30.666 --> 01:51:32.165
Tell me you're all right!

01:51:32.250 --> 01:51:33.707
Yeah, I'll be fine.

01:51:34.416 --> 01:51:36.790
Tch, you're wearing some sturdy armor.

01:51:37.250 --> 01:51:39.874
Fine, the next one will kill you.

01:51:40.375 --> 01:51:42.957
No, I'll protect Neia with my life.

01:51:43.416 --> 01:51:44.416
What?

01:51:45.791 --> 01:51:48.082
And did you notice the bow she's using?

01:51:48.333 --> 01:51:50.749
It's a masterpiece
loaned to her by Lord Ainz.

01:51:51.000 --> 01:51:52.000
What?

01:51:52.791 --> 01:51:54.249
From the Sorcerer King?

01:51:54.458 --> 01:51:57.124
That's right, made with Rune technology.

01:51:57.375 --> 01:51:59.499
Shizu, don't reveal all our secrets!

01:51:59.750 --> 01:52:00.750
It can’t be.

01:52:01.166 --> 01:52:05.207
You mean the secret weapon-making technique
that was thought to have been lost to time?

01:52:06.041 --> 01:52:07.999
A weapon like that is so valuable.

01:52:08.791 --> 01:52:10.790
It might even kill a great demon like me!

01:52:10.875 --> 01:52:12.290
I don't know what's going on here.

01:52:12.375 --> 01:52:13.375
A Rune weapon!

01:52:13.583 --> 01:52:15.165
Never thought I would see the day!

01:52:15.250 --> 01:52:15.749
What are Runes?

01:52:16.000 --> 01:52:17.000
It doesn't matter!

01:52:17.083 --> 01:52:18.374
It’s just a nice bow!

01:52:23.458 --> 01:52:24.165
Runes, though!

01:52:24.208 --> 01:52:25.208
Shut up!

01:52:26.875 --> 01:52:28.540
Well, all right then.

01:52:29.916 --> 01:52:30.916
Blindness.

01:52:31.250 --> 01:52:32.250
I can't see!

01:52:32.375 --> 01:52:33.915
It's fine, just shoot.

01:52:34.208 --> 01:52:35.208
Right!

01:52:39.166 --> 01:52:40.166
Well done!

01:52:40.583 --> 01:52:41.124
Huh?

01:52:41.541 --> 01:52:42.582
I hit it?

01:52:42.708 --> 01:52:43.999
Let's keep on the offensive.

01:52:46.708 --> 01:52:48.540
Your Highness, we did it!

01:52:48.666 --> 01:52:49.666
We're free!

01:52:50.916 --> 01:52:52.290
Can you see now?

01:52:53.250 --> 01:52:55.249
Uh-huh, all better now.

01:52:56.625 --> 01:52:57.874
That's good to hear.

01:53:02.000 --> 01:53:04.290
I can't believe we pulled that off.

01:53:05.208 --> 01:53:06.457
Splendid work, my friends.

01:53:07.541 --> 01:53:11.249
Now, everyone, eat Grandmother's
corpse with the utmost of care.

01:53:12.708 --> 01:53:14.707
Wait, was it someone you knew?

01:53:15.000 --> 01:53:17.874
She was queen of a demi-human
tribe called the Pandax.

01:53:18.250 --> 01:53:20.540
She was also my childhood crush.

01:53:21.500 --> 01:53:24.249
I assume you’ll eat the
human head before we depart?

01:53:24.625 --> 01:53:27.832
Uh, no, that's not what we
humans do when people die.

01:53:29.166 --> 01:53:30.957
But I think we should take it home.

01:53:31.583 --> 01:53:32.583
Very well.

01:53:34.875 --> 01:53:36.957
Hey, Neia, our mission’s complete.

01:53:37.208 --> 01:53:38.957
I think we’d better get out of here.

01:53:39.291 --> 01:53:40.582
All right, let's go.

01:53:51.916 --> 01:53:53.582
Cut them all down

01:53:53.791 --> 01:53:55.790
Don't leave one demi-human alive!

01:53:55.916 --> 01:53:57.374
Other than the Zerns, that is!

01:53:58.000 --> 01:53:59.332
I know, I know!

01:54:02.125 --> 01:54:03.125
This is it!

01:54:03.291 --> 01:54:07.082
This is our chance to stand up for
justice with our own two hands!

01:54:44.041 --> 01:54:46.582
Humans, I have returned!

01:54:47.291 --> 01:54:51.165
Ah, I see you've chosen
a fine place to die!

01:54:54.041 --> 01:54:57.707
Seems that you’ve done as you
please while my injuries were healing.

01:54:58.041 --> 01:55:00.749
But all of your fun will
come to an end now.

01:55:04.583 --> 01:55:07.249
None shall escape my flames of wrath!

01:55:07.541 --> 01:55:10.040
Wrath and suffer till
naught but ash remains!

01:55:11.500 --> 01:55:12.500
Retreat from here!

01:55:12.583 --> 01:55:13.249
I’ll fight!

01:55:13.416 --> 01:55:14.082
You can't!

01:55:14.250 --> 01:55:14.957
That’s madness!

01:55:14.958 --> 01:55:15.540
You should run for your life!

01:55:15.541 --> 01:55:16.701
You should run for your life!

01:55:16.958 --> 01:55:17.958
I can't win.

01:55:18.000 --> 01:55:19.249
You're correct on that account.

01:55:19.666 --> 01:55:20.332
But that’s fine!

01:55:20.583 --> 01:55:23.624
So long as I can protect others,
I know what I am doing is just!

01:55:23.833 --> 01:55:26.207
And justice is something worth dying for!

01:55:27.208 --> 01:55:28.290
Very well, then.

01:55:28.625 --> 01:55:29.625
Let's go!

01:55:41.125 --> 01:55:42.125
Look, Neia;

01:55:43.500 --> 01:55:44.707
It can't be!

01:55:49.083 --> 01:55:51.624
Those are demi-human reinforcements!

01:55:51.708 --> 01:55:53.082
I have to notify the troops!

01:55:55.458 --> 01:55:56.458
Hurry up!

01:55:56.875 --> 01:55:57.875
Retreat now

01:55:58.875 --> 01:56:00.707
Demi-human troops are coming from the east!

01:56:00.958 --> 01:56:01.999
They have reinforcements!

01:56:02.333 --> 01:56:03.333
Oh no!

01:56:05.791 --> 01:56:08.040
Spread the word before
we get trapped in here!

01:56:08.750 --> 01:56:10.082
That cursed demon!

01:56:10.541 --> 01:56:12.874
How many pawns does he have to throw at us

01:56:13.375 --> 01:56:14.375
This is bad!

01:56:14.708 --> 01:56:17.749
They must have gathered all the
remaining demi-humans from Abilion Hills!

01:56:20.833 --> 01:56:22.707
You should escape while you still can!

01:56:22.958 --> 01:56:23.958
What about you?

01:56:24.208 --> 01:56:25.208
I’m not leaving!

01:56:27.500 --> 01:56:34.207
In the last battle, I wanted to stay by his majesty's
side, but I couldn’t because I was too weak!

01:56:34.916 --> 01:56:39.082
But as someone who served the Sorcerer
King, I can’t allow it to end that way!

01:56:39.541 --> 01:56:42.665
My weakness is a sin that I must atone for!

01:56:45.166 --> 01:56:47.624
He protected all of these people’s lives.

01:56:47.916 --> 01:56:50.415
I have to help them escape,
no matter what it takes’

01:56:51.041 --> 01:56:52.041
Listen, Shizu.

01:56:52.291 --> 01:56:54.499
I'll have to entrust my mission to you now.

01:56:55.041 --> 01:56:56.832
Find his majesty in my stead.

01:56:57.166 --> 01:56:58.457
That shouldn’t be hard.

01:56:59.791 --> 01:57:01.832
And I don't need to run away, either.

01:57:04.333 --> 01:57:05.333
Look there!

01:57:11.333 --> 01:57:12.790
The Sorcerer Kingdom!

01:57:13.291 --> 01:57:14.457
That's their flag!

01:57:25.000 --> 01:57:26.749
His majesty has returned!

01:57:27.250 --> 01:57:28.250
He's alright!

01:57:35.791 --> 01:57:39.749
What a coincidence meeting
you here, Miss Baraja.

01:57:40.500 --> 01:57:42.540
Did you think I was dead, perhaps?

01:57:43.166 --> 01:57:44.332
Of course not!

01:57:44.333 --> 01:57:45.790
I’m just glad to see you!

01:57:46.166 --> 01:57:47.415
I've never lost faith

01:57:47.666 --> 01:57:52.707
Shizu said you were fine and I believed her since
we're such good friends, but I'm just so overwhelmed!

01:57:54.750 --> 01:57:56.749
Heh, I see.

01:57:57.125 --> 01:57:58.499
I'm happy to hear that.

01:57:59.166 --> 01:58:01.124
But wait, you're friends?

01:58:01.541 --> 01:58:02.582
Please don't cry.

01:58:04.833 --> 01:58:09.332
Hmm, I see you and Shizu have
grown quite close, Miss Baraja.

01:58:09.750 --> 01:58:10.832
What a pleasant surprise.

01:58:11.458 --> 01:58:12.749
It's all thanks to your wisdom!

01:58:13.083 --> 01:58:14.499
You left me with a great partner!

01:58:14.750 --> 01:58:16.332
We bonded through our love for you!

01:58:16.833 --> 01:58:18.624
Seems you did well in my absence.

01:58:19.250 --> 01:58:20.957
Anything else you'd like to report?

01:58:21.458 --> 01:58:22.249
Hmm. Shizu?

01:58:22.250 --> 01:58:24.165
Neia is awesome.

01:58:24.833 --> 01:58:26.165
She has a unique face.

01:58:26.500 --> 01:58:27.582
What does that mean?

01:58:29.666 --> 01:58:33.499
Oh wait, I’ll save all of my
questions until the battle is over.

01:58:34.125 --> 01:58:35.125
But one thing.

01:58:35.708 --> 01:58:38.332
Are you angry that we took
so long to go search for you?

01:58:38.666 --> 01:58:40.874
If so, I will take full responsibility!

01:58:41.500 --> 01:58:43.332
Why, the thought never crossed my mind.

01:58:43.708 --> 01:58:47.582
Everything has worked out well enough, so
I have no reason to be angry with anyone.

01:58:49.250 --> 01:58:50.207
Your majesty...

01:58:50.208 --> 01:58:53.207
Rather, I apologize for making you wait.

01:58:55.125 --> 01:58:59.165
After I was defeated by
Jaldabaoth, I fell into the Abelion Hills.

01:58:59.583 --> 01:59:04.332
It took a bit of work on my part, but the entire
area is now under the rule of the Sorcerer Kingdom.

01:59:05.000 --> 01:59:08.999
In other words, all of the
forces here belong to me!

01:59:11.791 --> 01:59:16.790
Now, I do believe I have a bit of revenge
to take on our nemesis, Jaldabaoth.

01:59:23.416 --> 01:59:25.665
Hey, isn't that the Sorcerer King?

01:59:25.958 --> 01:59:27.374
He's alive after all!

01:59:27.750 --> 01:59:29.165
His majesty's here!

01:59:29.416 --> 01:59:30.624
The Sorcerer King!

01:59:31.458 --> 01:59:34.165
I can't help but notice that
they're calling my name.

01:59:34.416 --> 01:59:38.165
Of course, they're celebrating
the return of their hero after all.

01:59:38.500 --> 01:59:40.207
These people owe their lives to you.

01:59:41.000 --> 01:59:43.082
Is that really how they feel?

01:59:43.541 --> 01:59:45.874
The humans are thanking me?

01:59:46.208 --> 01:59:47.208
That's right!

01:59:47.250 --> 01:59:48.250
They love you!

01:59:48.916 --> 01:59:50.957
Courtesy of your influence, no doubt.

01:59:51.541 --> 01:59:54.582
It seems you’ve grown stronger
in my absence, Miss Baraja.

01:59:55.500 --> 01:59:56.749
Thank you, your majesty!

01:59:56.916 --> 01:59:58.540
I'm so honored that you think so!

02:00:02.291 --> 02:00:03.457
Listen well!

02:00:04.750 --> 02:00:07.582
Last time, I was taken by surprise.

02:00:08.041 --> 02:00:11.540
I was outnumbered and had
consumed much of my magic power.

02:00:12.166 --> 02:00:15.624
But tonight, the
circumstances are different.

02:00:16.041 --> 02:00:20.499
There is no one who can
defeat me at full strength!

02:00:20.958 --> 02:00:24.207
Wait here, and I shall return victorious!

02:00:35.750 --> 02:00:37.540
Fight well, your majesty!

02:00:38.125 --> 02:00:39.125
For justice!

02:00:39.875 --> 02:00:40.875
Indeed!

02:00:44.916 --> 02:00:46.582
I've kept you waiting.

02:00:51.583 --> 02:00:53.749
I failed to kill you last time.

02:00:53.916 --> 02:00:54.999
Not today.

02:01:41.791 --> 02:01:42.791
He won.

02:01:53.916 --> 02:01:55.124
And you were right!

02:01:55.666 --> 02:01:57.290
I told you so, trainee.

02:02:09.916 --> 02:02:11.915
Glory to his majesty!

02:02:12.333 --> 02:02:14.457
Praise the Sorcerer King!

02:02:24.083 --> 02:02:25.690
Royal Capital: Hoburns

02:02:25.714 --> 02:02:29.217
And that is how his majesty,
the sorcerer King defeated Jaldabaoth.

02:02:30.541 --> 02:02:34.874
After Kalinsha the Liberation Army pushed
forward and retook the city of Prart.

02:02:35.083 --> 02:02:39.040
Then, at long last, our kingdom's
capital, Hoburns, was liberated as well.

02:02:40.000 --> 02:02:42.499
His majesty, the Sorcerer
King, is without equal.

02:02:43.125 --> 02:02:46.832
He fought to bring us peace for the
people of this land and demi-humans too.

02:02:47.250 --> 02:02:48.957
Demihumans don't deserve peace!

02:02:49.250 --> 02:02:49.665
Of course, I think it's fair
for you to feel that way.

02:02:49.666 --> 02:02:51.957
Of course, I think it’s fair
for you to feel that way.

02:02:51.958 --> 02:02:53.624
They killed many people.

02:02:53.916 --> 02:02:54.999
We can't just forget.

02:02:55.541 --> 02:02:59.957
And yet, like us plenty of demi-humans
were also victims of Jaldabaoth.

02:03:00.625 --> 02:03:03.332
His majesty dealt with them,
but he did so with kindness.

02:03:04.000 --> 02:03:07.582
He delivered them from our kingdom
and let them live safely under his flag.

02:03:07.833 --> 02:03:11.207
Thus, we are protected too
and peace is preserved for all.

02:03:11.625 --> 02:03:19.625
Now, I ask, have you ever heard of a king who ventures out alone and puts his
life on the line for another kingdom just because its people are suffering?

02:03:19.791 --> 02:03:24.040
Have you ever heard of a king who shows
kindness to all no matter their race?

02:03:24.208 --> 02:03:27.915
Oh, uh, actually, when
you put it that way, no.

02:03:28.583 --> 02:03:29.082
And I agree!

02:03:29.208 --> 02:03:30.249
It’s just as you say!

02:03:33.958 --> 02:03:38.499
There should be no borders when it comes to
kindness, no borders when it comes to bravery.

02:03:40.541 --> 02:03:42.832
He showed me a new
way to look at the world.

02:03:43.416 --> 02:03:47.915
And that's why there’s none other like him,
why he is the one and only King of Justice.

02:03:47.916 --> 02:03:51.915
For what Gould be more just than
wielding strengthen the name of kindness?

02:03:52.833 --> 02:04:00.833
That is why this land and all of its people, why all people in the
world must seek peace beneath the great wings of the Sorcerer King!

02:04:03.000 --> 02:04:04.499
Another fine speech.

02:04:04.625 --> 02:04:06.165
You're spreading the good word.

02:04:06.416 --> 02:04:09.749
Well, my job is easy when his
majesty has accomplished so much.

02:04:10.083 --> 02:04:11.374
I don’t deserve credit.

02:04:12.625 --> 02:04:15.082
There's a matter I'd
like to discuss with you.

02:04:16.291 --> 02:04:18.874
His majesty's followers
have continued to grow.

02:04:19.166 --> 02:04:20.874
We're now 50,000 strong.

02:04:21.583 --> 02:04:23.082
That's so uplifting to hear!

02:04:23.541 --> 02:04:26.874
Bit by bit, people are starting to
understand his majesty's greatness.

02:04:27.833 --> 02:04:30.040
Although, that is only natural.

02:04:30.500 --> 02:04:33.290
He saved our kingdom from
complete destruction after all.

02:04:33.625 --> 02:04:41.165
Getting back to the matter I mentioned earlier, since our organization has grown
so much, the supporters would like to have some sort of symbol of their faith.

02:04:41.500 --> 02:04:42.500
Oh, I see.

02:04:42.541 --> 02:04:44.457
I must admit I hadn’t thought of that.

02:04:44.458 --> 02:04:46.249
Can I leave the matter to you?

02:04:46.708 --> 02:04:47.790
It would be my pleasure.

02:04:49.833 --> 02:04:51.165
I'll tell his majesty.

02:04:51.666 --> 02:04:53.749
I'm sure he’ll be as happy as we are.

02:04:56.916 --> 02:04:58.540
Are you certain, your majesty?

02:04:59.541 --> 02:04:59.915
Yes.

02:05:00.458 --> 02:05:03.082
That equipment is my gift
to you for all your hard work.

02:05:03.541 --> 02:05:05.749
You've made good
use of it already, after all.

02:05:06.791 --> 02:05:09.582
Now, I shall return to
the Sorcerer Kingdom.

02:05:10.125 --> 02:05:11.749
My business here has concluded.

02:05:12.083 --> 02:05:13.540
There’s nothing more I can say.

02:05:14.125 --> 02:05:16.415
Though I'm still sad you
can’t get a proper farewell.

02:05:16.833 --> 02:05:19.624
Since you saved us, you
deserve to be seen off like a hero.

02:05:20.500 --> 02:05:22.040
I assure you that's no concern.

02:05:22.583 --> 02:05:26.915
In fact, I specifically asked Prince
Caspond not to make a big affair of this.

02:05:27.500 --> 02:05:28.332
And yet...

02:05:28.333 --> 02:05:29.333
You're their savior.

02:05:29.500 --> 02:05:31.165
They wanted to express their thanks.

02:05:33.416 --> 02:05:34.749
Well, no need to linger.

02:05:36.041 --> 02:05:39.124
Shizu, do you have anything
you’d like to say to Miss Baraja?

02:05:40.416 --> 02:05:41.416
See you.

02:05:41.791 --> 02:05:42.165
All right.

02:05:42.666 --> 02:05:43.666
See you.

02:05:44.041 --> 02:05:47.582
I know your kingdom still has
many challenges left to overcome.

02:05:49.375 --> 02:05:52.665
However, I'm confident that you
have the strength to succed.

02:05:53.458 --> 02:05:54.040
Let us meet again someday

02:05:54.041 --> 02:05:55.081
Let us meet again someday.

02:05:57.166 --> 02:05:59.290
I do have one last question.

02:06:00.708 --> 02:06:02.499
Well, it's just...

02:06:03.625 --> 02:06:07.290
If you don't mind, would it be all
right if I call you Lord Ainz?

02:06:08.666 --> 02:06:09.207
Yes.

02:06:09.625 --> 02:06:12.165
If that would please you, I will allow it.

02:06:12.250 --> 02:06:13.250
Thank you very much!

02:06:13.541 --> 02:06:15.790
And Shizu, come back soon!

02:06:24.291 --> 02:06:25.999
Farewell, our hero!

02:06:26.750 --> 02:06:29.499
His Majesty, the Sorcerer King!

02:06:30.125 --> 02:06:31.125
Hooray!

02:06:48.125 --> 02:06:52.415
Lord Ainz, your kindness changed my life.

02:06:58.291 --> 02:07:04.290
From now on, with every ounce of my power, I’ll
spread your justice through the whole kingdom!

02:07:10.000 --> 02:07:16.582
Despite the fact that my leadership steered us through the war, I’m
sure plenty of nobles will be quite unhappy once I become Sacred King.

02:07:17.291 --> 02:07:22.249
Especially those in the Southern Territory, who
are far-away from most of the death and violence.

02:07:22.666 --> 02:07:27.707
As time goes on, discontent will grow sparking
a great rift between the North and South.

02:07:28.291 --> 02:07:31.832
Then, inevitably, the Sacred
Kingdom will be split in two.

02:07:33.833 --> 02:07:36.040
You honor me with your presence, my lord.

02:07:36.708 --> 02:07:37.874
How may I serve you?

02:07:38.666 --> 02:07:41.957
Just checking in, since I was
already here to seize some treasure.

02:07:43.000 --> 02:07:44.957
Have you encountered any problems thus far?

02:07:45.625 --> 02:07:46.874
Not at all, my lord.

02:07:47.416 --> 02:07:50.874
Everything has been proceeding
exactly according to your plans.

02:07:51.500 --> 02:07:51.915
Splendid.

02:07:52.208 --> 02:07:53.749
Then on to the next phase.

02:07:54.125 --> 02:07:57.499
Let us further aggravate the relationship
between the North and the South.

02:07:57.500 --> 02:07:59.207
Till we incite a civil war.

02:08:00.291 --> 02:08:05.832
Searching for hope, or searching for asylum, the
people of this land will naturally turn to Lord Ainz.

02:08:06.208 --> 02:08:09.665
Then, willfully, they shall give
themselves fully to the Sorcerer Kingdom.

02:08:10.625 --> 02:08:11.874
I do have one question.

02:08:12.500 --> 02:08:15.749
Is it safe to let Neia Baraja
continue with what she's doing?

02:08:16.458 --> 02:08:21.874
Even if she spreads support for His Majesty, I fear
her popularity may outweigh the Sacred Kings in time.

02:08:22.416 --> 02:08:23.416
Leave her be.

02:08:23.500 --> 02:08:29.249
Lord Ainz's actions may seem inscrutable at first, but
that is only because his true genius is beyond our ken.

02:08:30.083 --> 02:08:31.707
Pie has prepared a splendid pawn!

02:08:32.083 --> 02:08:35.457
I see that now, that the pieces
have fallen so neatly into place!

02:08:35.875 --> 02:08:39.457
This is a land mired in religion,
reliant on their sacred king.

02:08:39.791 --> 02:08:44.499
And yet Lord Ainz has effortlessly
forged the perfect loyal mouthpiece.

02:08:44.791 --> 02:08:46.957
One that will expedite my plan by years.

02:08:47.291 --> 02:08:51.540
To that end, he even staged his own
death, fooling the whole Sacred Kingdom.

02:08:52.125 --> 02:08:53.874
His genius is terrifying.

02:08:53.875 --> 02:08:57.874
Even amongst the Supreme Beings,
he stands atop the highest peak!

02:08:59.291 --> 02:09:03.457
Lord Ainz, I shall not rest till this
whole world is in your grasp.

02:09:04.791 --> 02:09:07.749
Now, any other questions
before I'm on my way?

02:09:08.333 --> 02:09:08.832
Yes.

02:09:09.208 --> 02:09:10.499
Remedios Custodio.

02:09:10.875 --> 02:09:12.582
She's no longer of any use to us.

02:09:12.791 --> 02:09:15.957
Would it not be safer just to kill her
before she causes more trouble?

02:09:16.500 --> 02:09:19.665
Well, I wouldn't say
she's completely useless.

02:09:20.208 --> 02:09:23.332
For now, she'll serve as a fine target
for the discontent of the nobles.

02:09:23.333 --> 02:09:27.124
We'll dispose of her once both sides have
thoroughly turned against one another.

02:09:28.125 --> 02:09:29.499
Very well, my lord.

02:09:31.291 --> 02:09:32.540
I’ll leave you to it.

02:09:37.708 --> 02:09:40.790
Enjoy your happiness while
you can, my dear subjects.

02:09:41.125 --> 02:09:42.874
You may find it is quite fleeting.

02:14:11.500 --> 02:14:15.707
Shizu, this is your
first time working solo.

02:14:15.958 --> 02:14:17.832
So how did it go?

02:14:18.916 --> 02:14:21.165
I think I did my best.

02:14:22.666 --> 02:14:25.999
But it's tough to think and act alone.

02:14:26.000 --> 02:14:28.415
It's really challenging.

02:14:29.083 --> 02:14:30.624
Y-Yeah, that's true.

02:14:31.500 --> 02:14:33.457
Right, Baraja is human,

02:14:33.458 --> 02:14:36.249
but it seems like you've
gotten quite close.

02:14:37.250 --> 02:14:38.915
She's my favorite.

02:14:40.125 --> 02:14:41.707
Oh, that's great to hear.

02:14:42.416 --> 02:14:45.415
By the way, how about the
rune+ sword I asked you about?

02:14:46.125 --> 02:14:47.207
Were there any who showed interest

02:14:47.208 --> 02:14:48.665
or wanted rune weapons?

02:14:48.666 --> 02:14:49.666
Did anyone express that?

02:14:50.791 --> 02:14:51.791
I did my best.

02:14:53.000 --> 02:14:55.374
I see, you really worked hard.

02:14:57.166 --> 02:14:58.166
I did my best.
